 Nacional (PAR) 1 - 1 San Lorenzo 2014-08-06 21:15:00\n2014 San Lorenzo 1 - 0 Nacional (PAR) 2014-08-13 21:15:00\n2015 Tigres 0 - 0 River Plate 2015-07-29 22:00:00\ngoals sample types: {'str'}\nnon-numeric goals: 2 [{'datetime': '2015-05-14 21:00:00', 'home_team': 'Boca Juniors', 'away_team': 'River Plate', 'home_goal': '-', 'away_goal': '-', 'season': '2015', 'stage': 'round of 16'}, {'datetime': 'NA', 'home_team': 'Flamengo', 'away_team': 'Athletico', 'home_goal': '-', 'away_goal': '-', 'season': 'NA', 'stage': 'final'}]\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"venv/bin/python -c \"\nimport csv\nwith open('data/kaggle/Libertadores_Matches.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    rows = list(csv.DictReader(f))\nna = [r for r in rows if r['season']=='NA']\nprint('NA season rows:', len(na)); print(na[:3])\nfin = [r for r in rows if r['stage']=='final']\nprint('finals:', len(fin)); \nfor r in fin[:5]: print(r['season'], r['home_team'], r['home_goal'], '-', r['away_goal'], r['away_team'], r['datetime'])\nprint('goals sample types:', set(type(r['home_goal']).__name__ for r in rows))\nodd = [r for r in rows if not r['home_goal'].strip().isdigit()]\nprint('non-numeric goals:', len(odd), odd[:3])\n\"","time":{"start":1788243798522,"end":1788243798525}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now I have a good understanding of the data. Let me check Libertadores 'NA' season rows and the fifa club names for Brazilian clubs, then design the implementation.\n\nKey design considerations:\n\n1. **Data layer** (`data_loader.py`): Load all 6 CSVs into unified Match and Player models. Normalize team names (strip state suffixes like \"-SP\", \" - RJ\", country indicators \"(URU)\", case variants like \"Abc - RN\" vs \"ABC - RN\", accents e.g. \"Atlético\" vs \"Atletico\"). Normalize dates to ISO. Handle Libertadores goals stored as strings \"2\", possibly \"NA\".\n\n2. **Normalization**: \n   - Strip accents (unicodedata NFD)\n   - Lowercase\n   - Remove state suffix patterns: `-SP`, ` - RJ`, `(URU)` etc.\n   - Map common variants: \"Atlético Mineiro\" -> \"Atletico-MG\"? Hmm, FIFA club names: \"Atlético Mineiro\" (Atletico-MG), \"Atlético Paranaense\" (Atletico-PR), \"Sport Club do Recife\" (Sport-PE), \"Ceará Sporting Club\" (Ceara-CE), \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" (America-MG). I need a canonical name mapping table for well-known clubs.\n\n3. **MCP server** (`server.py`): Using the `mcp` Python SDK with FastMCP. Tools:\n   - `search_matches` — by team(s), date range, competition, season, stage/round\n   - `get_head_to_head` — two teams head-to-head record\n   - `get_team_stats` — team statistics (season, competition, home/away filter)\n   - `search_players` — by name, nationality, club, position, min rating; sorted\n   - `get_standings` — competition standings for a season (calculated from matches)\n   - `get_competition_info` — seasons, matches, finals\n   - `get_statistics` — aggregate stats: avg goals, home win rate, biggest wins, best records\n   - `list_teams` / `list_competitions` — discovery helpers\n   - `find_player` — player lookup\n\n4. **Tests**: BDD GWT structured pytest (Given/When/Then style) — the prompts.txt mentions \"test using BDD GWT structured PyTest\". TASK.md says \"Use BDD (Behavior-Driven Development) test scenarios\". I'll write pytest tests with Given/When/Then structure in test functions using comments and BDD-style naming. The prompts.txt says to ignore it, but the TASK.md itself says \"Use BDD test scenarios\". I'll write pytest tests structured as GWT.\n\nAlso TASK.md says nothing about Neo4j specifically in TASK.md (that's in prompts.txt which is to be ignored). TASK.md says \"knowledge graph interface\" but the practical requirement is an MCP server with query tools. I'll build an in-memory graph-ish model (matches, teams, players) — no external DB dependency, since stack.json says \"tooling: none\". Keep it self-contained.\n\n5. **Performance**: load data once, index by team/season. Simple lookups < 2s, aggregates < 5s. With ~24k matches and 18k players, pure Python is fine.\n\nLet me check a few more data details:\n- Libertadores 'NA' season rows\n- Copa do Brasil round values (are finals marked?)\n- BR-Football ht_result/at_result values\n- FIFA Position values\n\nThen write the code. Let me also check what \"final\" stage looks like in Libertadores and Copa do Brasil rounds.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05ba2e9c7001DAI0KV1UZUM5kT","sessionID":"ses_fa45f1af7ffepwbxxISA0FiJ2d","messageID":"msg_05ba26eae001tN1lXrRmdbzaPn"}}
