{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788244164254,"sessionID":"ses_fa45f1af7ffepwbxxISA0FiJ2d","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_eabcdcf9ee564526bd5e9b3e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"venv/bin/python -c \"\nimport csv\nwith open('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    rows = list(csv.DictReader(f))\nimport collections\nc = collections.Counter((r['season'], r['round']) for r in rows)\nfor s in ['2020','2021']:\n    print(s, {r:n for (ss,r),n in c.items() if ss==s})\nlate = [r for r in rows if r['round'] in ('7','8')]\nprint(late[-4:])\n\""},"output":"2020 {'1': 40, '2': 20, '3': 20, '4': 10, '5': 16, '6': 8, '7': 4, '8': 2}\n2021 {'1': 40, '2': 20, '3': 32, '4': 16}\n[{'round': '7', 'datetime': '2020-12-23 21:30:00', 'home_team': 'Palmeiras - SP', 'away_team': 'America - MG', 'home_goal': '1', 'away_goal': '1', 'season': '2020'}, {'round': '7', 'datetime': '2020-12-30 21:30:00', 'home_team': 'America - MG', 'away_team': 'Palmeiras - SP', 'home_goal': '0', 'away_goal': '2', 'season': '2020'}, {'round': '8', 'datetime': '2021-02-28 21:00:00', 'home_team': 'Grêmio - RS', 'away_team': 'Palmeiras - SP', 'home_goal': '0', 'away_goal': '1', 'season': '2020'}, {'round': '8', 'datetime': '2021-03-07 18:00:00', 'home_team': 'Palmeiras - SP', 'away_team': 'Grêmio - RS', 'home_goal': '2', 'away_goal': '0', 'season': '2020'}]\n","metadata":{"output":"2020 {'1': 40, '2': 20, '3': 20, '4': 10, '5': 16, '6': 8, '7': 4, '8': 2}\n2021 {'1': 40, '2': 20, '3': 32, '4': 16}\n[{'round': '7', 'datetime': '2020-12-23 21:30:00', 'home_team': 'Palmeiras - SP', 'away_team': 'America - MG', 'home_goal': '1', 'away_goal': '1', 'season': '2020'}, {'round': '7', 'datetime': '2020-12-30 21:30:00', 'home_team': 'America - MG', 'away_team': 'Palmeiras - SP', 'home_goal': '0', 'away_goal': '2', 'season': '2020'}, {'round': '8', 'datetime': '2021-02-28 21:00:00', 'home_team': 'Grêmio - RS', 'away_team': 'Palmeiras - SP', 'home_goal': '0', 'away_goal': '1', 'season': '2020'}, {'round': '8', 'datetime': '2021-03-07 18:00:00', 'home_team': 'Palmeiras - SP', 'away_team': 'Grêmio - RS', 'home_goal': '2', 'away_goal': '0', 'season': '2020'}]\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"venv/bin/python -c \"\nimport csv\nwith open('data/kaggle/Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    rows = list(csv.DictReader(f))\nimport collections\nc = collections.Counter((r['season'], r['round']) for r in rows)\nfor s in ['2020','2021']:\n    print(s, {r:n for (ss,r),n in c.items() if ss==s})\nlate = [r for r in rows if r['round'] in ('7','8')]\nprint(late[-4:])\n\"","time":{"start":1788244164246,"end":1788244164252}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now `normalize.py` — the most delicate part. Requirements:\n\n1. `strip_accents`\n2. Detect and strip Brazilian state (UF) suffixes: \"-SP\", \" - RJ\", trailing \" PR\" word\n3. Detect and keep international country suffixes: \"-EQU\", \"(URU)\", \"-PAR\", \" (VEN)\" etc.\n4. Canonical alias table for well-known clubs mapping base names to canonical \"base-uf\" keys\n5. Display name beautification\n6. Date parsing: \"2023-09-24\", \"2012-05-19 18:30:00\", \"29/03/2003\", \"NA\", \"-\"\n7. Goal parsing: \"2\", 2, \"-\", \"NA\"\n\nCanonical key scheme:\n- Brazilian club: \"base-uf\" (e.g. \"flamengo-rj\", \"atletico-mg\", \"abc-rn\")\n- International: \"base\" (e.g. \"boca juniors\", \"river plate\") — but \"Nacional (URU)\" vs \"Nacional (PAR)\": key \"nacional-uru\" / \"nacional-par\"? If I keep 3-letter country codes as suffix, then \"Barcelona-EQU\" -> \"barcelona-equ\" which distinguishes from Spanish \"Barcelona\". Hmm, but FIFA \"FC Barcelona\" -> \"fc barcelona\" — different clubs anyway, no need to unify with Ecuadorian Barcelona. For simplicity: international clubs keep their country code in the key when present in the source. \"Guaraní (PAR)\" and \"Guaraní-PAR\" both -> \"guarani-par\" ✓. \"Libertad\" and \"Libertad-PAR\" — Libertad is Paraguayan; \"Libertad\" without suffix would key as \"libertad\" ≠ \"libertad-par\". Need alias: \"libertad\" -> \"libertad-par\"? But there could be multiple Libertads... In this dataset only Paraguay's Libertad appears. I'll add safe aliases where unambiguous. Actually simpler: for international clubs, the country suffix stays attached when present; when absent, plain base. Alias table unifies known important ones: \"libertad\" -> \"libertad\", hmm.\n\nWait — actually, do Libertadores \"Flamengo\" (no suffix) and Brasileirão \"Flamengo-RJ\" need to unify? Yes! That's the whole point of \"handles team name variations\". So Brazilian clubs: strip UF into a hint, then canonical key = base + \"-\" + uf where uf comes from (a) explicit suffix, (b) alias default, (c) dataset context. \n\n\"Athletico\" (Libertadores 2021 final, no suffix) — alias \"athletico\" -> \"atletico-pr\" (since Athletico-PR is the same club as Atletico-PR; base \"atletico\" with uf \"pr\"). Hmm wait: \"Atletico-PR\" -> base \"atletico\", uf \"pr\" -> key \"atletico-pr\". \"Athletico Paranaense\" (FIFA) -> base \"athletico paranaense\" -> alias -> \"atletico-pr\". \"Atlético Paranaense\" -> alias -> \"atletico-pr\". ✓.\n\n\"Atlético-MG\" -> \"atletico-mg\". \"Atlético Mineiro\" -> alias \"atletico mineiro\" -> \"atletico-mg\". \"Atletico Mineiro\" (BR-Football) -> \"atletico-mg\" ✓.\n\nAmbiguity risk: \"Atletico\" alone with no uf and no alias default — e.g. Copa do Brasil \"Atlético - AC\" (Atletico Acreano), \"Atletico - ES\"? Those have explicit UFs so fine. If a name is exactly \"Atletico\" with no suffix anywhere: Libertadores 2021 \"Athletico\" (alias handles), and \"Real Atlético\" (Bolivia) stays \"real atletico\" ✓ distinct.\n\nPlan for `canonical_team_key(raw)`:\n1. `clean = strip_accents(raw).lower().strip()`\n2. Remove parenthetical content, but first capture it: if parenthetical is a 3-letter country code (URU, PAR, EQU, VEN, PER, ARG, CHI, COL, BOL, MEX) → country = that code. Other parentheticals (\"(antigo Esporte Clube Barreira)\", \"(Minas Gerais)\") are dropped.\n3. Detect trailing UF: regex ` - (uf)$` or `-(uf)$` where uf in UFS, or trailing standalone word uf (` coritiba pr$`). Remove → base, uf.\n   Wait, careful with trailing word: \"4 de julho - pi\" handled by \" - pi\". \"Coritiba PR\" → \"coritiba pr\" → trailing word \"pr\" is UF → base \"coritiba\". But what about a team legitimately ending in a UF-looking word without being a suffix? e.g. none realistically.\n4. Detect trailing 3-letter country code: `-(xxx)$` where xxx in COUNTRY_CODES → country.\n5. base cleanup: remove punctuation (\"a.b.c.\" → \"abc\"), collapse spaces, strip \"ec\"/\"fc\"? No — keep. Hmm \"Botafogo\" vs \"Botafogo PB\"? Copa do Brasil has \"Botafogo - PB\" presumably with suffix — fine, distinct key \"botafogo-pb\". FIFA \"Botafogo\" → alias default rj → \"botafogo-rj\" ✓.\n6. Look up base in ALIASES: maps base → (canonical_base, default_uf or None).\n   - \"atletico mineiro\" → (\"atletico\", \"mg\")\n   - \"atletico paranaense\" / \"athletico paranaense\" / \"athletico\" → (\"atletico\", \"pr\")\n   - \"flamengo\" → (\"flamengo\", \"rj\")\n   - \"sao paulo\" / \"sao paulo fc\" → (\"sao paulo\", \"sp\")\n   - \"vasco\" / \"vasco da gama\" → (\"vasco\", \"rj\")\n   - \"sport\" / \"sport club do recife\" / \"sport do recife\" / \"sport recife\" → (\"sport\", \"pe\")\n   - \"ceara\" / \"ceara sporting club\" → (\"ceara\", \"ce\")\n   - \"america\" default? AMBIGUOUS (MG and RN and CE). No default. \"america fc\" (FIFA, after dropping \"(Minas Gerais)\") → alias (\"america fc\" → (\"america\", \"mg\")). Hmm, \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" — parenthetical \"(minas gerais)\" is not a code; dropped → base \"america fc\" → alias → (\"america\",\"mg\") ✓. \"América - MG\" → base \"america\", uf \"mg\" ✓. \"America-MG\" ✓. \"América - RN\" → (\"america\",\"rn\") ✓. \"América de Natal\" → alias → (\"america\",\"rn\")? América de Natal is