"brasiliense\" → (\"brasiliense\",\"df\"); \"ipatinga\" → (\"ipatinga\",\"mg\").\n\n   Also BR-Football teams without accents and sometimes with suffix words: \"Atletico Mineiro\" (alias ✓), \"Atletico Goianiense\" → (\"atletico\",\"go\")? alias \"atletico goianiense\" → (\"atletico goianiense\",\"go\")? Hmm — Atletico-GO in Brasileirão file is \"Atletico-GO\" → base \"atletico\", uf \"go\" → \"atletico-go\". For BR-Football \"Atletico Goianiense\" to unify, alias → (\"atletico\",\"go\") ✓. Similarly \"atletico acreano\"? distinct club (Série C) — that's Atlético-AC; alias (\"atletico\",\"ac\")? But wait \"Atlético - AC\" in Copa do Brasil → base \"atletico\", uf \"ac\" → \"atletico-ac\" ✓ and BR-Football \"Atletico Acreano\" → alias → \"atletico-ac\" ✓. \n\n   \"Atletico Alagoinhas\" (BA, Série C)? → (\"atletico\",\"ba\")? Atlético de Alagoinhas is BA. OK.\n   Hmm, this could go deep. The core requirement: \"Handles team name variations correctly\" for major clubs and exact-normalized matches for the rest. Perfect unification of every tiny Série C club across files is out of scope; I'll cover all Série A regulars + notable others + generic rules.\n\n7. Final key: if uf → f\"{canonical_base}-{uf}\"; elif country → f\"{canonical_base}-{country}\"; else canonical_base. Also if alias provides default_uf and no explicit uf → use default.\n\nAlso `team_display_name(key)` → prettified display: I'll maintain a display map built from the most common raw name per key during loading (first-seen with UF-suffix style). Simpler: store display name = the raw name as it appears in the dataset when first registered, preferring accented versions. E.g. key \"flamengo-rj\" first seen in Brasileirão file as \"Flamengo-RJ\" → display \"Flamengo-RJ\"? Spec answers use \"Flamengo\". Hmm. For display in match listings I use the raw names from the match itself (home_team/away_team as recorded) — that's authentic. For team stats answers, display via a prettifier: title-case base + \" (UF)\"? I'll build display from a curated dict for major clubs and fall back to title-casing the key's base. Let me keep a DISPLAY_NAMES dict for ~60 major clubs: \"flamengo-rj\": \"Flamengo\", \"atletico-mg\": \"Atlético Mineiro\", etc.\n\nDate parsing:\n- \"2012-05-19 18:30:00\" → datetime → date\n- \"2023-09-24\" → date\n- \"29/03/2003\" → date (DD/MM/YYYY)\n- \"NA\", \"\", \"-\" → None\n\nGoal parsing: int if digit; \"-\" / \"NA\" / \"\" → None.\n\nCompetition canonical names:\n- COMPETITION names: \"Brasileirão Série A\", \"Brasileirão Série B\", \"Brasileirão Série C\", \"Copa do Brasil\", \"Copa Libertadores\".\n- Source mapping:\n  - Brasileirao_Matches.csv → \"Brasileirão Série A\"\n  - novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv → \"Brasileirão Série A\"\n  - BR-Football: \"Serie A\" → \"Brasileirão Série A\", \"Serie B\" → \"Brasileirão Série B\", \"Serie C\" → \"Brasileirão Série C\", \"Copa do Brasil\" → \"Copa do Brasil\"\n  - Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv → \"Copa do Brasil\"\n  - Libertadores_Matches.csv → \"Copa Libertadores\"\n\nCompetition aliases for queries: \"brasileirao\", \"serie a\", \"campeonato brasileiro\" → Brasileirão Série A; \"libertadores\" → Copa Libertadores; \"copa do brasil\" → Copa do Brasil; \"serie b\", etc.\n\nRound/stage: Brasileirão round int; Copa do Brasil \"round\" 1-8 (8 = final rounds? rounds 1-8; actually Copa do Brasil has rounds: 1st round... final is \"Final\"? here rounds are 1-8, presumably 8th round ~ semifinal/final?). Let me check what round the Copa do Brasil final matches are: 2021 final (Athletico-PR vs Flamengo) — let me check. Also stage strings in Libertadores: \"final\", \"semifinals\", etc. For \"find all Copa do Brasil finals\" I need to detect finals: round 8? Let me check quickly in data.\n\nDerbies (clássicos) mapping (by canonical keys):\n- Fla-Flu: flamengo-rj / fluminense-rj\n- Clássico dos Milhões: flamengo-rj / vasco-rj\n- Clássico Vovô: botafogo-rj / fluminense-rj? Actually Botafogo vs Fluminense is \"Clássico Vovô\".\n- Derby Paulista: corinthians-sp / palmeiras-sp (Derby Paulista), Choque-Rei: corinthians-sp / sao paulo-sp, Majestoso: sao paulo-sp / palmeiras-sp? (Majestoso is São Paulo vs Corinthians? No — Majestoso is São Paulo x Corinthians? Let me get these right:\n  - Derby Paulista: Palmeiras x Corinthians ✓\n  - Choque-Rei: São Paulo x Palmeiras? No, Choque-Rei is São Paulo x Santos? Hmm. Let me recall: \"Choque-Rei\" is São Paulo x Palmeiras? Actually: Choque-Rei = São Paulo vs Palmeiras? I believe Choque-Rei is São Paulo x Palmeiras. And \"Majestoso\" is São Paulo x Corinthians. \"Clássico Alvinegro\" São Paulo x Santos? No that's \"Clássico dos Milhões\"? no. Brafter checking: \n    - Majestoso: Corinthians x São Paulo ✓\n    - Choque-Rei: Palmeiras x São Paulo ✓\n    - Clássico dos Milhões: Santos x Santos? no. Let me just include the well-known ones:\n  - Gre-Nal: Internacional x Grêmio ✓\n  - Clássico Mineiro (O Clássico das Multidões): Atlético-MG x Cruzeiro ✓\n  - Ba-Vi: Bahia x Vitória ✓\n  - Clássico-Rei / Re-Pa: Remo x Paysandu (not in data probably)\n  - Clássico dos Gigantes: Vasco x Flamengo? Actually \"Clássico dos Milhões\" = Flamengo x Vasco ✓\n  - Clássico Vovô: Botafogo x Fluminense ✓\n  - Leão x Parreira? no.\n  - Atle-Tiba: Atlético-PR x Coritiba ✓\n  - Cope-Rio? Fla-Flu is \"Clássico das Multidões\"? Fla-Flu = \"O Clássico das Multidões\" — yes! And \"Clássico dos Milhões\" is Flamengo x Vasco. OK.\n  \n  I'll include: Fla-Flu (flamengo/fluminense), Clássico dos Milhões (flamengo/vasco), Derby Paulista (palmeiras/corinthians), Majestoso (corinthians/sao paulo), Choque-Rei (palmeiras/sao paulo), Gre-Nal (gremio/internacional), Clássico Mineiro (atletico-mg/cruzeiro), Ba-Vi (bahia/vitoria), Atle-Tiba (atletico-pr/coritiba), Clássico Vovô (botafogo/fluminense), Clássico Alvinegro Carioca? botafogo/vasco = \"Clássico dos Rivais\"? skip.\n\nCopa do Brasil finals: let me check the round values for known finals quickly. Also I need to double check \"Ath