ys both home and away (impossible) — the elif logic was defensive nonsense. Also `_by_comp_season` should include ALL matches even with no date/season (the NA Libertadores final). Let me fix that block.\n\nAlso `find_team` has a subtle issue: `needle in base or base in needle` — \"atletico\" query → base \"atletico\" matches keys atletico-mg, atletico-pr, atletico-go, atletico-ac... ranked by match_count. Good. But also `base in needle`: query \"Clube Atlético Paranaense\" → key canonical → alias → \"atletico-pr\" exact ✓.\n\nQuery \"América\" → key \"america\" (no uf, no alias default since \"america\" not in aliases) → exact miss (teams are america-mg, america-rn, america-ce?), substring: base \"america\" in needle \"america\" ✓ → matches all americas ranked by matches. Good.\n\nEdge: query \"Sport\" → alias (\"sport\",\"pe\") → key \"sport-pe\" exact ✓. But \"Sport\" query might also mean \"Sport Recife\" ✓ same.\n\nEdge: query \"Santos\" → \"santos-sp\" ✓. But \"Santos Laguna\" (Mexican, in FIFA & Libertadores) → key \"santos laguna\" — needle \"santos\" in \"santos laguna\" ✓ → included as candidate ranked below santos-sp probably (fewer matches: Santos FC has thousands of matches, Laguna has ~dozens in FIFA players only + Libertadores matches vs Brazilian teams... maybe 0 matches, only players). Good.\n\nNow fix the index build block.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05bac27d8001BVXHtnLIWN7sFf","sessionID":"ses_fa45f1af7ffepwbxxISA0FiJ2d","messageID":"msg_05babbf44001eIyXUJTlHkoTz1"}}
