etort-80ffd0e4ce9f/data_loader.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/data_loader.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/data_loader.py\n@@ -149,9 +149,11 @@\n existing = self._dedup.get(dedup_key)\n if existing is not None:\n     kept = self.matches[existing]\n     if not kept.stats and match.stats:\n-        self.matches[existing] = replace(kept, stats=match.stats)\n+        merged = replace(kept, stats=match.stats)\n+        self.matches[existing] = merged\n+        self.stats_matches.append(merged)\n     return\n self._dedup[dedup_key] = len(self.matches)\n self.matches.append(match)\n if match.stats:\n","additions":3,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"data_loader.py","time":{"start":1788244444272,"end":1788244444274}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Wait, there's a bug with stats_matches: in `_add_match`, when a match is added, if it has stats it goes to stats_matches. But when a dedup happens and stats get merged into the kept match, the kept match is replaced but stats_matches still references the old object. Let me look:\n\n```python\nif match.stats:\n    self.stats_matches.append(match)\n```\nand in dedup branch, `self.matches[existing] = replace(kept, stats=match.stats)` — but if `kept` was in stats_matches already (it wouldn't be if it had no stats... `if not kept.stats and match.stats` — kept has no stats, so kept was never added to stats_matches; the new `match` (with stats) was appended to stats_matches BEFORE the dedup check? No wait — order in `_add_match`:\n\n```python\ndef _add_match(self, match):\n    ...register teams...\n    dedup_key = ...\n    existing = self._dedup.get(dedup_key)\n    if existing is not None:\n        kept = self.matches[existing]\n        if not kept.stats and match.stats:\n            self.matches[existing] = replace(kept, stats=match.stats)\n        return          <-- early return BEFORE stats append\n    self._dedup[dedup_key] = len(self.matches)\n    self.matches.append(match)\n    if match.stats:\n        self.stats_matches.append(match)\n```\n\nHmm, but when merged, the stats live in self.matches[existing] but stats_matches never gets it. stats_matches is only used for corner/shot stat queries; slightly incomplete. Simpler: don't maintain a separate stats_matches list — compute from self.matches when needed (rare queries, 24k scan is fast). Or in the dedup branch, also append the merged match to stats_matches. Let me just append the replaced match to stats_matches in the dedup branch.\n\nAlso the ordering issue: `self.matches.sort(...)` in _build_indexes after players load — fine.\n\nLet me update the dedup branch.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05bacc462001I3Nv9h5n7mhtVc","sessionID":"ses_fa45f1af7ffepwbxxISA0FiJ2d","messageID":"msg_05bac73d4001k5LUJGctqdp3eZ"}}
