ate, home_key, away_key). For the same match in Brasileirao_Matches (2019) and novo (2019): date should match... but novo dates are \"29/03/2003\" style DD/MM/YYYY parsed ✓. Hmm, but wait — maybe the dates DIFFER between sources for the same fixture (data errors/different recorded dates). Or home/away keys differ?\n\nAlso \"2020 relegated\" shows 'Fortaleza Fc' — different key for Fortaleza! BR-Football has \"Fortaleza Fc\" or \"Fortaleza EC\"? canonical_team_key(\"Fortaleza FC\") → base \"fortaleza fc\" — not in aliases (I have \"fortaleza ec\" but maybe the raw is \"Fortaleza Fc\"). Fix: add \"fortaleza fc\" → (\"fortaleza\",\"ce\"). Similarly other \"Fc\"/\"EC\" variants. Let me check what raw names exist for these teams.\n\nAlso relegated 2020 shows Fortaleza twice (once as \"Fortaleza\", once as \"Fortaleza Fc\") — confirming key mismatch → dedup failed for Fortaleza matches too (two entries for the same match with different keys!). Wait no — dedup failed because the KEYS differ, so the same match from two files created two entries with different keys. That inflates standings.\n\nRoot causes to fix:\n1. Add missing club alias variants (Fortaleza Fc, etc.).\n2. Check date mismatches between sources for the same fixture.\n\nFor (2): Brasileirao_Matches 2019 vs novo 2019 — same fixture may have slightly different dates between Kaggle datasets (e.g. one says Sat, other says Sun). If dates differ, dedup by (date, home, away) fails. More robust dedup: (competition, season, home_key, away_key, round) — round number should be stable within a season for Série A! For Copa do Brasil (two legs same round possible) — no: round 8 final has TWO legs (home/away). Key (comp, season, home_key, away_key, round) for the final: leg1 Grêmio x Palmeiras round 8, leg2 Palmeiras x Grêmio round 8 — different home/away → distinct keys ✓. But round 3 could have same pairing twice? No, each round is one match per pairing except finals (2 legs, reversed venues — distinct keys). \n\nHmm wait, but is that safe for Libertadores? Libertadores uses stage, not round. Group stage: same pairing twice (home and away legs) — distinct keys via home/away swap ✓. Knockouts: 2 legs, swapped venues ✓. But same-stage rematch with same venue? No. OK.\n\nFor BR-Football (no round), season derived from date.year. Copa do Brasil 2020 final played in Feb 2021 → season=2021 in BR-Football vs season=2020 in Brazilian_Cup. Dedup key (comp, season, home, away, round): rounds differ (None vs \"Final\") → NOT deduped. Hmm. But for Copa do Brasil, priority source (Brazilian_Cup) has season 2020 ✓ and BR-Football duplicate would appear as a separate 2021 season match. Copa do Brasil 2021 season then includes some 2020-final duplicates. Minor, acceptable — but let me improve: for dedup, use season-less key (comp, home_key, away_key, date)? The problem was date mismatch. Combine: primary key (comp, date, home, away); fallback fuzzy key for same-season pairing: (comp, season, home, away, round-ish). \n\nSimplest robust approach: dedup on (comp, home_key, away_key, date) OR (comp, home_key, away_key, season, round). I.e., check both keys. Two matches same teams same season same round = same match even if date differs slightly. Two matches same teams same date = same match even if season/round differ.\n\nLet me implement: `_dedup` maps both key variants → index. On add:\n- k1 = (comp, date, home, away) — only if date is not None\n- k2 = (comp, season, home, away, round_label) — only if season and (round or stage) present\n- if either key exists → merge stats and return\n- else register both keys.\n\nFor BR-Football (no round): k2 = (comp, season, home, away, None) — season from year. Two DIFFERENT matches same teams same season? Copa do Brasil early rounds: teams meet twice? In rounds 1-2 it's single-leg. Later rounds 2 legs — reversed home/away, distinct keys. Serie A: home/away reversed, distinct. OK but there's a subtle case: Copa do Brasil rounds 1/2 — single match; but with k2=(comp, season, home, away, None) — if two different one-leg matches with same venue pairing same season... doesn't happen.\n\nBUT: BR-Football Copa do Brasil vs Brazilian_Cup same match: BR-Football k2 = (\"Copa do Brasil\", 2021, palmeiras-sp, gremio-rs, None) vs Brazilian_Cup k2 = (\"Copa do Brasil\", 2020, ..., \"Final\") — no match! And k1 date: both have same date (2021-02-28, 2021-03-07) presumably ✓ — if dates agree, k1 catches it. If dates differ, duplicate. Let me check whether the dates agree for those finals.\n\nAlso: same-date two matches in different seasons of same comp: k1 (comp, date, home, away) — a Série A match Palmeiras x Santos on 2019-08-04 (season 2019) and another on 2020-08-04? Different dates. Fine.\n\nAlso nuevo vs Brasileirao same season 2012-2019: k2 catches with same round numbers. Let me verify rounds match between files: novo Rodada 1-38, Brasileirao round 1-38 ✓ hopefully consistent.\n\nLet me first diagnose: check Fortaleza variants and date mismatches.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05bb0424e0013aPpfjPgYKwABn","sessionID":"ses_fa45f1af7ffepwbxxISA0FiJ2d","messageID":"msg_05baf6502001uhrqXCa7Aqxo33"}}
