items():\n    with open(path, encoding='utf-8-sig') as f:\n        rows = list(csv.DictReader(f))\n    sets[name] = keys_from_pairs([(r[h], r[a]) for r in rows])\n\ndef base(k): return k.rsplit('-',1)[0]\n# cross-file near matches: same base, different key, or base of one equals/contains base of other\nnames = list(sets)\nfor i, n1 in enumerate(names):\n    for n2 in names[i+1:]:\n        conflicts = []\n        for k1 in sets[n1]:\n            for k2 in sets[n2]:\n                if k1 == k2: continue\n                b1, b2 = base(k1), base(k2)\n                if b1 == b2 or (b1 and b1 in b2) or (b2 and b2 in b1):\n                    conflicts.append((k1, k2))\n        if conflicts:\n            print(f'--- {n1} vs {n2}: {len(conflicts)}')\n            for c in conflicts[:15]: print('   ', c)\n\" 2>&1 | head -70","time":{"start":1788244799698,"end":1788244799702}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"OK, most of these are small Série C clubs unique to BR-Football (no cross-file matching needed — they only appear in one file, so their key form doesn't matter). The important ones for cross-file unification are clubs appearing in MULTIPLE files:\n\nKey ones to alias:\n- \"Fortaleza FC\" → (\"fortaleza\",\"ce\") — critical (Série A + Libertadores)\n- \"Vitoria EC\" → (\"vitoria\",\"ba\") — Série B club\n- \"Santa Cruz FC\" → (\"santa cruz\",\"pe\")\n- \"Nautico Capibaribe\" → (\"nautico\",\"pe\") — hmm, is \"Nautico Capibaribe\" in BR-Football AND \"Náutico\" in novo? Yes likely.\n- \"CA Parana\" → (\"parana\",\"pr\")\n- \"America FC Natal\" → (\"america\",\"rn\")\n- \"CS Alagoano\"? that's CSA! \"CS Alagoano\" → (\"csa\",\"al\")\n- \"Novorizontino\" → (\"red bull bragantino\"? NO! Novorizontino is Grêmio Novorizontino — a different club from Red Bull Bragantino. Both exist. \"Gremio Novorizontino\" and \"Novorizontino\" are the same club (Série B). Alias \"novorizontino\" → (\"gremio novorizontino\",\"sp\")? Hmm what key do I want: \"gremio novorizontino-sp\". And \"Grêmio Novorizontino\" in other files? Probably only in BR-Football. Let me set alias \"gremio novorizontino\" → (\"gremio novorizontino\",\"sp\") and \"novorizontino\" → (\"gremio novorizontino\",\"sp\").\n- \"Clube Do Remo\" → (\"remo\",\"pa\"); \"Remo\" appears as bare \"remo\" — key \"remo\". Alias \"remo\" → (\"remo\",\"pa\"), \"clube do remo\" → (\"remo\",\"pa\"). Paysandu → (\"paysandu\",\"pa\").\n- \"Portuguesa Desportos\" → (\"portuguesa\",\"sp\")\n- \"Ferroviario\" → (\"ferroviario\",\"ce\")\n- \"Caxias\" → (\"caxias\",\"rs\"); SER Caxias. \"Brasil de Pelotas\" → (\"brasil de pelotas\",\"rs\") (Brasil-RS vs \"Brasil de Pelotas\" same club).\n- \"CRB\" → (\"crb\",\"al\")\n- \"Vila Nova\" → (\"vila nova\",\"go\"); \"Villa Nova\" (MG) → (\"villa nova\",\"mg\") distinct ✓.\n- \"Ituano\" → (\"ituano\",\"sp\"); \"Sao Bento\"? keep. \"Oeste\" → (\"oeste\",\"sp\")? Oeste-SP. \"Santo Andre\" → (\"santo andre\",\"sp\"). \"Sao Caetano\" → (\"sao caetano\",\"sp\"). \"Guaratingueta\" → (\"guaratingueta\",\"sp\")? Hmm — do these appear in other files? Probably not. Adding default UFs for known clubs is harmless and helps queries like \"Ituano\".\n- \"Londrina\" → (\"londrina\",\"pr\"), \"Maringa\" → (\"maringa\",\"pr\"), \"Cianorte\" → (\"cianorte\",\"pr\"), \"Tombense\" → (\"tombense\",\"mg\"), \"Tupi\" → (\"tupi\",\"mg\"), \"Uberlandia\" → (\"uberlandia\",\"mg\"), \"Caldense\" (\"caldense\",\"mg\"), \"Boa\" (\"boa\",\"mg\")? Boa Esporte-MG ✓. \"Pouso Alegre\" (\"pouso alegre\",\"mg\")? fine.\n- \"Sampaio Correa\" → (\"sampaio correa\",\"ma\"), \"Tuna Luso\" (\"tuna luso\",\"pa\"), \"Mixto\" (\"mixto\",\"mt\").\n- \"Confianca\" (\"confianca\",\"se\"), \"AD Confianca\" → (\"confianca\",\"se\").\n- \"CRAC\" (\"crac\",\"go\"), \"Goianesia\" (\"goianesia\",\"go\"), \"Anapolina\" (\"anapolina\",\"go\"), \"Anapolis FC\" → (\"anapolis\",\"go\")? Hmm \"Anápolis\" in Copa do Brasil → \"anapolis-go\"; alias \"anapolis fc\" → (\"anapol