\"pa\"), \"remo\" → (\"remo\",\"pa\")\n- \"duque de caxias fc\" → (\"duque de caxias\",\"rj\")\n- \"ferroviario\" → (\"ferroviario\",\"ce\")\n- \"brasil de pelotas\" → (\"brasil de pelotas\",\"rs\")\n- \"brasilia fc\" → (\"brasilia\",\"df\")\n- \"gremio novorizontino\" → (\"gremio novorizontino\",\"sp\"), \"novorizontino\" → (\"gremio novorizontino\",\"sp\")\n- \"fc atletico cearense\" → (\"atletico cearense\",\"ce\")\n- remove \"red bull brasil\" alias (keep as its own club — pre-2019 entity)\n\nAlso add DISPLAY_NAMES for new keys where useful, and fix `_TRAILING_WORD_RE` handling: \"america mg\" — trailing word \"mg\" is a UF ✓ auto. \"guarani sp\" ✓ auto.\n\nNow the dual-key dedup in data_loader. Implement in `_add_match`:\n\n```python\ndef _add_match(self, match):\n    register teams...\n    keys = []\n    if match.date is not None:\n        keys.append((\"date\", match.competition, match.date, match.home_key, match.away_key))\n    label = match.round or match.stage\n    if match.season is not None and label:\n        keys.append((\"round\", match.competition, match.season, match.home_key, match.away_key, label))\n    for k in keys:\n        if k in self._dedup:\n            existing = self._dedup[k]\n            kept = self.matches[existing]\n            merge stats...\n            return\n    idx = len(self.matches)\n    self.matches.append(match)\n    if match.stats: self.stats_matches.append(match)\n    for k in keys: self._dedup[k] = idx\n```\n\nWait, edge: BR-Football has no round/stage → label None → only date key. If a BR-Football match's date disagrees with the priority source's date AND has no round → duplicate remains. How common? Let me check after implementing: count Série A per season — should be 380 per season (except 2016: 380? Série A had 20 teams since 2006 → 380). Let me validate post-fix.\n\nAlso the round label for novo is \"Round N\" — novo Rodada for the same match as Brasileirao round should agree (verified 379/380 matching on (home,away,round) — one non-matching pair, probably a data discrepancy in one file; that match will dedupe via date key if dates agree).\n\nCopa do Brasil: BR-Football matches have no round → date key only. Check dates agreement for Copa do Brasil 2014-2021 between files.\n\nAlso potential false-positive dedup: two genuinely different matches with same (comp, date, home, away)? Impossible in practice.\n\nAnd (comp, season, home, away, round) false positives: Série A 2020 vs 2021 same fixture? No — season in key. Round labels unique per fixture per season ✓. Libertadores stage: two group-stage matches with SAME home/away in same season? No (home and away legs are reversed) ✓. Knockout same stage, same home team twice? Only if 2-leg with same venue — Copa do Brasil finals are home/away ✓.\n\nOne more: BR-Football \"Serie B\"/\"Serie C\" vs no other source — no dedup risk. Copa do Brasil in both cup file and BR-Football — the round labels: cup file rounds mapped to \"Round 1\"..\"Final\" via normalize_round; BR-Football has no round → skipped. Date key only. Fine.\n\nAlso I realize the Libertadores NA row: date None, season None, stage \"final\" → keys = [] → always added (no dedup possible). It's the only such row ✓.\n\nNow, also fix `_build_indexes` match_count: a team playing in match counted once home once away — can't happen. OK.\n\nLet me now rewrite BASE_ALIASES additions in normalize.py.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05bb47522001IX1bthn4UwNr02","sessionID":"ses_fa45f1af7ffepwbxxISA0FiJ2d","messageID":"msg_05bb3c9e1001hNc24C2LIGSJFt"}}
