n\nBut careful about a subtle issue: two different real matches same pairing 2 days apart — does that occur in the data? Série A: no (round-robin, each pairing once per direction per season). Série B/C same. Copa do Brasil: finals 2 legs, reversed venues. Libertadores: group stage legs reversed venues; knockouts reversed. So safe.\n\nImplementation: in _add_match, build probe keys: for d in [date-1, date, date+1] → (\"date\", comp, d, home, away). If any exists → merge. When storing, store under exact date key only. Since load order is brasileirao → novo → copa → libertadores → brfootball, and the ±1 probe is symmetric-ish: novo loads before brfoot; novo vs brasileirao disagreed dates by 1 day in 2 cases (2019) — probe catches those too ✓.\n\nWhat about BR-Football vs novo? novo only 2003-2019, BR-Football starts 2014 — overlap 2014-2019: dedup via ±1 day probe ✓ (round key: novo has \"Round N\" label, brfoot none → only date key).\n\nAlso 2020: champion wrong because duplicates inflated Atlético-MG. After fix, 2020 should be 380 matches, champion Flamengo.\n\nLet me also double check the 2016 Série A: real 2016 had 20 teams, 380 matches. But wait — 2016 had a match... let me just run after the fix. Also check 2021: 541 → should drop to 380 (Brasileirao has 2021 ✓).\n\nNote: 2023: 377 matches — season incomplete in BR-Football (data through Dec 2023, maybe missing last rounds). Fine.\n\nAlso Copa do Brasil 2020 final in Feb 2021: BR-Football season 2021 vs cup file season 2020 → same date ±1 probe catches it if dates agree ✓.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05bb7f842001oPAZXNXGTYW16z","sessionID":"ses_fa45f1af7ffepwbxxISA0FiJ2d","messageID":"msg_05bb739af001t4gjki7RrGjRmw"}}
