{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788245234853,"sessionID":"ses_fa45f1af7ffepwbxxISA0FiJ2d","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_9ca956fa240c485cb822fb1c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"venv/bin/python -c \"\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom data_loader import get_data, SERIE_A\ndata = get_data()\nfor season in (2016, 2022):\n    ms = data.matches_by_competition(SERIE_A, season)\n    print(season, 'by source:', Counter(m.source for m in ms))\n    per_team = Counter()\n    for m in ms:\n        per_team[m.home_key] += 1; per_team[m.away_key] += 1\n    odd = {t: n for t, n in per_team.items() if n != 38}\n    print('  teams != 38 games:', odd)\n    pairs = Counter((m.home_key, m.away_key) for m in ms)\n    dups = [(p, n) for p, n in pairs.items() if n > 1]\n    print('  dup pairings:', dups[:6])\n\""},"output":"2016 by source: Counter({'Brasileirao_Matches.csv': 380, 'BR-Football-Dataset.csv': 1})\n  teams != 38 games: {'brasilia-df': 1, 'ca taguatinga': 1}\n  dup pairings: []\n2022 by source: Counter({'Brasileirao_Matches.csv': 380, 'BR-Football-Dataset.csv': 1})\n  teams != 38 games: {'goias-go': 39, 'corinthians-sp': 39}\n  dup pairings: [(('goias-go', 'corinthians-sp'), 2)]\n","metadata":{"output":"2016 by source: Counter({'Brasileirao_Matches.csv': 380, 'BR-Football-Dataset.csv': 1})\n  teams != 38 games: {'brasilia-df': 1, 'ca taguatinga': 1}\n  dup pairings: []\n2022 by source: Counter({'Brasileirao_Matches.csv': 380, 'BR-Football-Dataset.csv': 1})\n  teams != 38 games: {'goias-go': 39, 'corinthians-sp': 39}\n  dup pairings: [(('goias-go', 'corinthians-sp'), 2)]\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"venv/bin/python -c \"\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom data_loader import get_data, SERIE_A\ndata = get_data()\nfor season in (2016, 2022):\n    ms = data.matches_by_competition(SERIE_A, season)\n    print(season, 'by source:', Counter(m.source for m in ms))\n    per_team = Counter()\n    for m in ms:\n        per_team[m.home_key] += 1; per_team[m.away_key] += 1\n    odd = {t: n for t, n in per_team.items() if n != 38}\n    print('  teams != 38 games:', odd)\n    pairs = Counter((m.home_key, m.away_key) for m in ms)\n    dups = [(p, n) for p, n in pairs.items() if n > 1]\n    print('  dup pairings:', dups[:6])\n\"","time":{"start":1788245234823,"end":1788245234851}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Excellent! Now the standings match real history:\n- 2019: Flamengo 90 pts ✓ (real: 90), Santos 74 ✓\n- 2020: Flamengo 71 ✓ (real: 71), Internacional 70 ✓\n- 2021: Atlético Mineiro 84 ✓ (real: 84), Flamengo 71 ✓\n- 2022: Palmeiras 66? hmm wait — real 2022: Palmeiras champion with 81 points! 66 is wrong. 2022 Série A: Palmeiras 81, Internacional 68? Hmm. Wait, actually no — 2022 Série A final standings: Palmeiras 81 pts. Hmm, but we got Palmeiras 66 with only 381 matches... hmm 381? Odd number. Wait 2022: 20 teams → 380. 381 suggests a dup or an extra. And champion 66 pts is too low.\n\nHmm wait, let me think. Maybe BR-Football 2022 Serie A data is incomplete (they had 377 for 2023). 66+... let me check match count per team in 2022. Actually wait — 2022 in real life: Palmeiras 81 pts (26W 3D... no: 23W 12D 3L = 81). We computed 66 = e.g. 19W 9D 10L. That's way off — suggests we're MISSING matches (377-ish season) — no wait, we have 381 matches which is MORE than 380.\n\nHmm, hold on. Maybe the 2022 season in BR-Football is actually incomplete (mid-season snapshot — the file may end in Dec 2023 but 2022 might be truncated). If only ~330 matches of 2022 present, standings would be off. But 381 > 380... Let me check: count by source and per-team match counts for 2022.\n\nAlso 2003: 552 matches — 2003 Série A really had 46 games per team (22 teams, 46 rounds = 1122 matches? no wait 22 teams × 46/2 = 506? Hmm). 2003: 24 teams, 46 rounds → 552 matches ✓ (24×46/2 = 552) ✓ correct! Cruzeiro 100 pts ✓ real (Cruzeiro won with 100+? Real 2003: Cruzeiro champion with 100 pts? Yes, Cruzeiro had 100 points in 2003 — hmm, actually I recall Cruzeiro 2003: 31W 7D 8L? 46 games → 100 pts ✓ plausible).\n\n2005: 462 matches — 2005 had 22 teams, 42 rounds → 462 ✓ Corinthians champion ✓ real.\n\n2016: 381 — hmm, 1 extra? 2016: Palmeiras champion ✓ 80 pts... real 2016: Palmeiras 78? Palmeiras 2016: 24W 11D 3L? Hmm no. Real: Palmeiras 78 pts (23W 9D 6L)? Let me check: 2016 Palmeiras: W23 D9 L6 = 78. We got 80. Hmm 381 matches — one extra match inflating points.\n\nLet me check 2016 and 2022 anomalies. 2022 might have a data quirk in BR-Football. Let me investigate both.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05bb8d0f1001p0zs2SU21hWJir","sessionID":"ses_fa45f1af7ffepwbxxISA0FiJ2d","messageID":"msg_05bb852b2001C8XxOb4bhC4kUR"}}
