{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788245269979,"sessionID":"ses_fa45f1af7ffepwbxxISA0FiJ2d","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_cc052d6fc44249f48f1e46bd","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"venv/bin/python -c \"\nfrom data_loader import get_data, SERIE_A\ndata = get_data()\nfor m in data.matches_by_competition(SERIE_A, 2022):\n    if (m.home_key, m.away_key) == ('goias-go','corinthians-sp'):\n        print(m.date, m.score, m.round, m.source, m.stats.get('home_corners'))\nfor m in data.matches_by_competition(SERIE_A, 2016):\n    if 'taguatinga' in m.home_key + m.away_key:\n        print(m.date, m.home_team, m.score, m.away_team, m.source)\n\""},"output":"2022-10-15 None Round 32 Brasileirao_Matches.csv None\n2022-10-29 0-0 None BR-Football-Dataset.csv 2\n2016-01-30 Brasilia FC 1-1 CA Taguatinga BR-Football-Dataset.csv\n","metadata":{"output":"2022-10-15 None Round 32 Brasileirao_Matches.csv None\n2022-10-29 0-0 None BR-Football-Dataset.csv 2\n2016-01-30 Brasilia FC 1-1 CA Taguatinga BR-Football-Dataset.csv\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"venv/bin/python -c \"\nfrom data_loader import get_data, SERIE_A\ndata = get_data()\nfor m in data.matches_by_competition(SERIE_A, 2022):\n    if (m.home_key, m.away_key) == ('goias-go','corinthians-sp'):\n        print(m.date, m.score, m.round, m.source, m.stats.get('home_corners'))\nfor m in data.matches_by_competition(SERIE_A, 2016):\n    if 'taguatinga' in m.home_key + m.away_key:\n        print(m.date, m.home_team, m.score, m.away_team, m.source)\n\"","time":{"start":1788245269951,"end":1788245269978}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Two data quirks:\n\n1. 2016: BR-Football has \"Brasilia\" vs \"CA Taguatinga\" match categorized as Serie A 2016 — these are Série B/C clubs! It's a BR-Football data error (mis-labeled tournament or a Copa Verde match?). It adds a fake Série A match. Should I filter? It's one match. This is the data's fault. I could leave it — standings unaffected (neither team is in Série A 2016 otherwise... but it pollutes the standings table with Brasília/Taguatinga entries). Hmm.\n\n2. 2022: Goiás x Corinthians appears twice — BR-Football 2022 has it at a different date (probably rescheduled match, played twice in reality? No...). Wait — Goiás x Corinthians 2022: there was a match POSTPONED and rescheduled. Maybe BR-Football has both the original date and the rescheduled date? Or my dedup failed because dates differ by more than 1 day. The ±1 probe didn't catch it. Real 2022 Série A: Goiás 1-0 Corinthians? and Corinthians 1-0 Goiás (reverse). If same-direction twice with different dates → the +1 probe misses.\n\nOptions:\na) Add a third dedup key: (comp, season, home, away, home_goals, away_goals) — same-direction pairing with identical score in same season = same match (with high probability). Risk: two different matches same season, same direction, same score — e.g., Copa do Brasil group... Copa do Brasil has no groups; Série A each direction once. Libertadores group stage: each direction once. Knockout: each direction once per stage but stage label in key. So (comp, season, home, away, score) is a strong identity! Two-leg ties with same score both legs (e.g., 1-0, 1-0 with reversed venues) → different directions → distinct keys ✓.\n\n   Edge: Libertadores 2019 Semifinal: Grêmio x Flamengo 1-0 and Flamengo x Grêmio 1-0? Different directions ✓ fine.\n\n   But hmm — what about Copa do Brasil matches where BOTH legs have same home team? Rare (both legs at same stadium happens for stadium-sharing teams? e.g. two Rio teams playing both legs at Maracanã — the \"home\" designation still alternates in the data). OK.\n\nb) Filter the 2016 Brasília x Taguatinga mis-categorized match: if a Série A season match involves a team with only 1 match in that competition — that's a data error, but hard to generalize. Alternative: hard-filter known bad row? Hacky but data-driven: I could drop matches where BOTH teams have < 3 matches in that competition+season... Actually a principled rule: for league competitions (Série A/B/C), a valid participant plays ≥ 10 matches in the season. Filtering mis-categorized rows this way is defensible: \"league seasons with fewer than 10 matches for a team indicate data errors in the source\".\n\nHmm, but that would also drop legitimately incomplete data (e.g., 2023 season 377 matches — teams still have 35+). And future partial data. The rule: drop league matches where either team plays < 5 matches in that competition-season. 2016 Brasília (1 match) → dropped ✓. 2023 teams have ~35 → kept ✓.\n\nLet me check what 2022's duplicate is exactly and whether the score-key approach catches it. Also check for other same-direction duplicate pairings across league seasons to validate approach (a).","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05bb95a1f001bn1VlrhUHIaASa","sessionID":"ses_fa45f1af7ffepwbxxISA0FiJ2d","messageID":"msg_05bb8d5f0001EHjuAqtE5oc0VU"}}
