G 2022 round 31\n   2022-10-09 18:00:00 Atletico-MG Ceara-CE 2022 round 31\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"venv/bin/python -c \"\nimport csv\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom normalize import parse_int\nwith open('data/kaggle/Brasileirao_Matches.csv', encoding='utf-8-sig') as f:\n    rows = list(csv.DictReader(f))\nunscored = [r for r in rows if parse_int(r['home_goal']) is None or parse_int(r['away_goal']) is None]\nprint('unscored Brasileirao rows:', len(unscored))\nfor r in unscored[:10]: print('  ', r['datetime'], r['home_team'], r['away_team'], r['season'], 'round', r['round'])\n\" ","time":{"start":1788245335598,"end":1788245335601}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"1. 2022 Goiás x Corinthians: the Brasileirão file says Round 32 on 2022-10-15 with NO score (score missing — probably unplayed at data cutoff, goals empty). BR-Football has the actual played match on 2022-10-29, 0-0. So these are the SAME fixture — Brasileirao file records it as unscored! The dedup missed it because... wait, the round-key: Brasileirao has \"Round 32\", BR-Football has no round. Date keys differ by 14 days. So it wasn't deduped.\n\nInteresting — how many Brasileirao_Matches rows have missing scores? If Brasileirao file has unscored matches (postponed/abandoned), and BR-Football has the actual result, we should MERGE rather than duplicate. Let me check for unscored matches in Brasileirao file.\n\n2. 2016 Brasília x Taguatinga: a mis-categorized match (it's from Campeonato Brasiliense or Copa Verde, labeled Serie A in BR-Football; date Jan 30, before Série A started in May).\n\nFixes:\n- For dedup: add score-based key (comp, season, home, away, home_goals, away_goals) when all present. The Brasileirao 2022 round-32 row has NO score → can't match by score. Hmm. But wait — the deduped match would keep the Brasileirao unscored version and never merge the BR-Football result. Better approach for unscored rows: \n  - Key idea: if a