, ('tupi-mg', 'londrina-pr'), 2), ('Brasileirão Série C', 2015, ('londrina-pr', 'tupi-mg'), 2), ('Brasileirão Série C', 2016, ('boa-mg', 'juventude-rs'), 2)]\n\nBrasileirão Série C 2014 total: 81 small: {'botafogo-pb': 7, 'aguia de maraba': 3, 'cuiaba-mt': 2, 'salgueiro-pe': 7, 'duque de caxias-rj': 5, 'crb-al': 3, 'macae-rj': 4, 'treze': 2}\nBrasileirão Série C 2015 total: 157 small: {'villa nova': 3, 'aguia de maraba': 7}\nBrasileirão Série C 2016 total: 181 small: {'ypiranga': 7}\nBrasileirão Série C 2021 total: 216 small: {'vila nova-go': 4, 'brusque': 3, 'remo-pa': 4, 'londrina-pr': 3}\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"venv/bin/python -c \"\nfrom collections import Counter\nfrom data_loader import get_data, SERIE_A, SERIE_B, SERIE_C, COPA_DO_BRASIL, LIBERTADORES\ndata = get_data()\n# check same-pairing same-direction duplicates with both scored (cup comps)\nfor comp in (COPA_DO_BRASIL, LIBERTADORES, SERIE_A, SERIE_B, SERIE_C):\n    dups = 0; examples = []\n    for season in data.seasons_for_competition(comp):\n        ms = [m for m in data.matches_by_competition(comp, season) if m.score]\n        pairs = Counter((m.home_key, m.away_key) for m in ms)\n        for p, n in pairs.items():\n            if n > 1:\n                dups += 1\n                if len(examples) < 3: examples.append((comp, season, p, n))\n    print(comp, 'same-direction dup pairings (both scored):', dups, examples)\nprint()\n# Série C small team-seasons\nfor season in data.seasons_for_competition(SERIE_C):\n    ms = data.matches_by_competition(SERIE_C, season)\n    per = Counter()\n    for m in ms: per[m.home_key]+=1; per[m.away_key]+=1\n    small = {t: n for t, n in per.items() if n < 8}\n    if small: print(SERIE_C, season, 'total:', len(ms), 'small:', small)\n\"","time":{"start":1788245395420,"end":1788245395448}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Findings:\n1. 82 unscored Brasileirão rows — mostly 2022 round 31+ (the dataset was captured mid-season 2022? but 2022 had 380 total... wait, Brasileirao_Matches has 2022 with unscored rounds 29-38, AND BR-Football has the completed 2022 season). Hmm — but 2022 standings showed Palmeiras 66 pts with 381 matches, meaning many 2022 Série A matches came from the unscored Brasileirao rows (no result → not counted in standings!) and BR-Football provided ~?? completed ones. Wait — if Brasileirao 2022 has 380 rows but many unscored, and BR-Football has the completed season, dedup matched the scored ones; unscored Brasileirao rows whose played version exists in BR-Football at a DIFFERENT date (rescheduled) remained unscored → standings missed them. E.g. Goiás x Corinthians: Brasileirao unscored Round 32 (10-15) + BR-Football played (10-29). The result: 2022 standings incomplete.\n\nSo the unscored-fixtures merge is essential. Design:\n- After primary dedup (probe keys fail), when adding a NEW match that HAS a score, check `unscored_index` for (comp, season, home, away): if the stored unscored match exists → REPLACE it in place (keep round/stage/stadium if missing on new).\n- When adding a match WITHOUT a score, record it in `unscored_index` (first only), and add to matches list (as unscored).\n- Also probe: when adding a scored match and an unscored version was already added → replace. Reverse order: scored added first, unscored arrives later → dedup keys would... the unscored match has same round label? Brasileirao unscored has Round 32 label; if BR-Football scored arrived FIRST (load order: brasileirao first!). Load order is brasileirao → novo → copa → libert → brfoot. So unscored Brasileirao rows are added FIRST, then scored BR-Football versions arrive → replacement path is the one needed. But also: unscored Brasileirao 2016 round 38 (Chapecoense, post-plane-crash canceled match — never played!). That one has no BR-Football counterpart (2016 not fully in BR-Football? BR-Football starts 2014, 2016 Serie A partially?). It stays unscored forever — correct! (The Chapecoense round 38 match vs Atlético-MG in 2016 was officially canceled after the plane crash.)\n\nSo replacement logic:\n```python\ndef _add_match(self, match):\n    ...register teams...\n    if match has score:\n        probe dedup keys (date±1, round) → merge stats if found, return\n        probe unscored dict (comp, season, home, away) → if found:\n            replace self.matches[idx] with merged (prefer match's score, keep round/stage from old if new missing)\n            remove from unscored dict (so a second played match same pairing... shouldn't happen)\n            merge stats into stats_matches if match.stats\n            return\n        add normally\n    else:\n        # unscored match: probe dedup keys too (if a scored version already exists, skip adding unscored)\n        probe dedup keys → if found: return (scored version already there; don't overwrite)\n        probe scored-with-same-pairing? (comp, season, home, away) — if a scored match exists with same identity, skip. Need scored_index dict[(comp,season,home,away)] = idx? Hmm — could a pairing occur twice same season same direction with one scored one unscored? The Goiás case in reverse order. Since load order is fixed (brasileirao before brfoot), unscored-first is the actual case. But to be safe both directions, maintain `pairing_index[(comp, season, home, away)] = (idx, has_score)`. On add:\n          - if pairing exists:\n              - existing unscored + new scored → replace\n              - existing scored + new unscored → drop new\n              - existing scored + new scored → normal dedup already handled (date/round) — if date/round differ AND both scored: keep first (data conflict, e.g. a true duplicate we can't detect) — the pairing_index prevents a second same-pairing match... WAIT DANGER: legitimate same-pairing same-direction twice in one season exists?? Copa do Brasil: hmm. Let me check the current deduped data: for cup comps, count (comp, season, home, away) occurrences > 1 with both scored.\n\nLet me check before implementing: in the deduped matches, same (comp, season, home, away, both scored) count > 1?\n\n2. Mis-categorized matches: Série A: exactly 2 team-seasons with 1 game (Brasília, Taguatinga 2016) → these come from ONE match. Série B: 7 team-seasons with 1 game + 1 with 2 → mis-categorized matches too. Série C: several small counts (2-7 games) — Série C seasons are partial in BR-Football (1807/10 = 180 per season; real Série C 2014+ had 20+ teams → 190+ matches minimum per season... 180 might be complete-ish for some formats?). Hmm wait, Série C 2020-2023 format: 20 teams, 19 rounds = 190 matches. 2014-2019: 22 teams? Let me check Série C per-season counts and formats. Actually — the partial-data question matters for the filter threshold. Teams with 2-7 games in Série C could be either (a) partial season data, or (b) mis-categorized matches.\n\nLet me look at which Série C team-seasons have small counts and whether they look like real Série C participants.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05bbb4444001iaI4MeKUJm36Nd","sessionID":"ses_fa45f1af7ffepwbxxISA0FiJ2d","messageID":"msg_05bba7101001q8IzUJGCdIr1xI"}}
