erie B Luverdense 1.0 - 1.0 Vila Nova\n2017-06-03 Serie B Vila Nova 3.0 - 1.0 Guarani SP\n2017-05-27 Serie B ABC 1.0 - 0.0 Vila Nova\n2017-05-20 Serie B Vila Nova 0.0 - 0.0 EC Juventude\n2017-05-13 Serie B Boa 0.0 - 1.0 Vila Nova\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"venv/bin/python -c \"\nimport csv\nwith open('data/kaggle/BR-Football-Dataset.csv', encoding='utf-8-sig') as f:\n    for r in csv.DictReader(f):\n        if r['tournament']=='Serie B' and r['date'][:4] in ('2017','2019','2022') and any(k in (r['home']+r['away']) for k in ('ragantino','Suzano','Macae','Monsoon','Bage','Tupi','Vila','Villa')):\n            print(r['date'], r['tournament'], r['home'], r['home_goal'], '-', r['away_goal'], r['away'])\n\"","time":{"start":1788245489847,"end":1788245489849}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Interesting — BR-Football names like \"Botafogo RJ\", \"Vasco Da Gama RJ\", \"URT MG\" — with UF as trailing word! My trailing-word UF detection handles \"Botafogo RJ\" → (\"botafogo\",\"rj\") ✓, \"Vasco Da Gama RJ\" → base \"vasco da gama\" + uf rj → key \"vasco da gama-rj\"?? WAIT — canonical_team_key strips the UF then looks up BASE_ALIASES: base \"vasco da gama\" → alias (\"vasco\",\"rj\") ✓ → \"vasco-rj\" ✓ good.\n\n\"Bragantino PA\" — trailing \"PA\"?? \"Bragantino PA\" is... Águia de Marabá? No — \"Bragantino PA\" = Bragantino-PA (Clube Atlético Bragantino? no, that's SP). There's a small PA club \"Bragantino\" (Bragantino Clube do Pará)! So \"Bragantino\" bare → my alias maps to red bull bragantino-sp — WRONG for \"Bragantino PA\" (explicit uf PA wins → \"bragantino-pa\"? base \"bragantino\" → alias (\"red bull bragantino\",\"sp\") but uf explicit \"pa\" → \"red bull bragantino-pa\"?? BAD!). \n\nHmm — alias mapping with explicit conflicting UF: if explicit uf ≠ alias default uf, the explicit should WIN and the BASE should stay unmapped: i.e., for \"Bragantino PA\": base \"bragantino\", alias → (\"red bull bragantino\",\"sp\"), but uf \"pa\" conflicts with \"sp\" → treat as a DIFFERENT club: keep base \"bragantino\" with uf \"pa\" → \"bragantino-pa\". I need to modify canonical_team_key: when alias has default_uf and explicit uf is present and they differ → don't remap base, use (original base, explicit uf).\n\nLet me also check \"URT MG\" → \"urt-mg\" ✓ fine. \"EC Juventude\" → \"ec juventude\" — not in aliases! Add \"ec juventude\" → (\"juventude\",\"rs\") ✓ I have \"ec juventude\" already ✓.\n\nWhat about \"Bragantino\" appearing in Série B 2017? The counts above only show Copa do Brasil. The Série B \"Red Bull Bragantino 2017 (1 match)\" — hmm, where's that from? Earlier scan of Série B by key showed 'red bull bragantino-sp': 1 in 2017. BR-Football raw must be \"Red Bull Brasil\"?? No wait, I removed that alias. \"Red Bull Brasil\" → key \"red bull brasil\"... The Série B 2017 1-match team was 'red bull bragantino-sp' — from raw \"Red Bull Brasil\"? Let me search... Actually earlier alias had \"red bull brasil\" → I REMOVED it, so \"Red Bull Brasil\" → key \"red bull brasil\". Then where does 'red bull bragantino-sp' with 1 Série B 2017 match come from? Maybe raw \"Bragantino\" in a Série B 2017 match... wait no, that would key to (\"red bull bragantino\",\"sp\") via alias ✓ — 1 match only. But real RB Bragantino played 38 Série B 2017 games as \"Bragantino\"? Hmm, 2017: the club was still \"Bragantino\" (Red Bull took over in 2019). Let me check BR-Football Série B 2017 for Bragantino raws.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05bbcb864001miuH5F7p4IyXGh","sessionID":"ses_fa45f1af7ffepwbxxISA0FiJ2d","messageID":"msg_05bbc47e20012KRHebvMC5ykOa"}}
