{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788245549068,"sessionID":"ses_fa45f1af7ffepwbxxISA0FiJ2d","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_369a66f477644cb3b38213c4","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/normalize.py","newString":"    base = _clean_base(base)\n    if not base:\n        return \"\"\n\n    if base in BASE_ALIASES:\n        canonical_base, default_uf = BASE_ALIASES[base]\n        if uf and default_uf and uf != default_uf:\n            pass\n        else:\n            base = canonical_base\n            uf = uf or default_uf\n\n    if uf:\n        return f\"{base}-{uf.lower()}\"\n    if country:\n        return f\"{base}-{country.lower()}\"\n    return base","oldString":"    base = _clean_base(base)\n    if not base:\n        return \"\"\n\n    if base in BASE_ALIASES:\n        base, default_uf = BASE_ALIASES[base]\n        uf = uf or default_uf\n\n    if uf:\n        return f\"{base}-{uf.lower()}\"\n    if country:\n        return f\"{base}-{country.lower()}\"\n    return base"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/normalize.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/normalize.py\n@@ -352,10 +352,14 @@\n if not base:\n     return \"\"\n \n if base in BASE_ALIASES:\n-    base, default_uf = BASE_ALIASES[base]\n-    uf = uf or default_uf\n+    canonical_base, default_uf = BASE_ALIASES[base]\n+    if uf and default_uf and uf != default_uf:\n+        pass\n+    else:\n+        base = canonical_base\n+        uf = uf or default_uf\n \n if uf:\n     return f\"{base}-{uf.lower()}\"\n if country:\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/normalize.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/normalize.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/normalize.py\n@@ -352,10 +352,14 @@\n if not base:\n     return \"\"\n \n if base in BASE_ALIASES:\n-    base, default_uf = BASE_ALIASES[base]\n-    uf = uf or default_uf\n+    canonical_base, default_uf = BASE_ALIASES[base]\n+    if uf and default_uf and uf != default_uf:\n+        pass\n+    else:\n+        base = canonical_base\n+        uf = uf or default_uf\n \n if uf:\n     return f\"{base}-{uf.lower()}\"\n if country:\n","additions":6,"deletions":2},"truncated":false},"title":"normalize.py","time":{"start":1788245549063,"end":1788245549066}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Very informative:\n- 2019-05-04 \"Suzano SP 3-0 Guarulhos SP\" labeled Serie B — clearly a mis-categorized Campeonato Paulista/Série D match. Same pattern as GE Bage 0-0 Monsoon (2022 Serie B — that's actually... hmm, GE Bagé and Monsoon are tiny RS clubs — mis-categorized).\n- \"Bragantino\" 2017 appears only once in Série B 2017 (2017-07-08 vs Tupi) — real Bragantino played all 38. So BR-Football's Série B 2017 is itself partial?? Wait no — looking at 2017 rows: only ~40 matches shown with Bragantino/Vila Nova. Vila Nova has ~37 ✓ full. Bragantino only 1 — the BR-Football 2017 Série B data seems partially complete... Actually no: BR-Football Série B 2017 should have 380 matches. The scan only matched rows containing my keywords — Bragantino appears in just 1 Série B 2017 row. Weird but it's the source's problem: their 2017 Série B is missing most Bragantino matches, OR Bragantino's matches are recorded under a different name. Whatever — source data quality; not my job to fabricate.\n- \"Villa Nova\" (2 matches in Série B 2017) vs \"Vila Nova\" — data entry variants of the SAME club (Vila Nova-GO)! \"Villa Nova\" (MG club) is Série C, but in Série B context it's clearly Vila Nova-GO mispelled. My alias: \"villa nova\" → (\"villa nova\",\"mg\") is WRONG for these rows. Hmm — \"Villa Nova\" in Série B 2017 = Vila Nova-GO. But Copa do Brasil 2015 \"Villa Nova\" = Villa Nova-MG (Série C). Ambiguous! Resolution: alias \"villa nova\" → NO default (keep \"villa nova\" as its own key)? Or map to MG? The BR-Football Série B rows would then split Vila Nova into \"vila nova-go\" + \"villa nova\". Since \"villa nova\" appears only 3 times total (2 Série B 2017 + 1 Copa 2015), minimal impact either way. Better: remove the \"villa nova\"→MG alias so it stays its own key \"villa nova\"; the MG club's other appearances? \"Villa Nova MG\"? Not seen. Keep it simple: no alias for \"villa nova\".\n\nWait, actually I never added a \"villa nova\" alias — I only added \"vila nova\" → (\"vila nova\",\"go\"). ✓ fine as-is. \"Villa Nova\" → key \"villa nova\" (no suffix, no alias) — stays separate from \"vila nova-go\". The 2 Série B 2017 matches get their own row in standings. Minor.\n\n- \"Botafogo SP\" — Botafogo-SP (Ribeirão Preto) → key \"botafogo-sp\" ✓ distinct from \"botafogo-rj\" ✓ correct!\n- \"Operario PR\" → \"operario-pr\" ✓; \"Tombense MG\" → \"tombense-mg\" ✓; \"URT MG\" → \"urt-mg\" ✓. Trailing-word UF works.\n- \"Bragantino PA\" (Copa 2019) → PROBLEM: alias maps base \"bragantino\" → (\"red bull bragantino\",\"sp\") with uf \"pa\" → currently produces \"red bull bragantino-pa\". Must fix: explicit UF conflicting with alias default → keep original base. Fix in canonical_team_key.\n- \"Atletico Goianiense\" 2019 Série B ✓ alias → atletico-go ✓.\n- \"America MG\" ✓ alias.\n- \"EC Juventude\" ✓ alias.\n\nFixes to make:\n1. canonical_team_key: when alias default_uf conflicts with explicit uf → don't remap base (use original base + explicit uf).\n2. The unscored-fixture merge (Brasileirão unscored 2022 Round 29-38 + BR-Football played versions).\n3. Mis-categorized league matches (teams with exactly 1 match in a league season): drop. — Suzano x Guarulhos (Série B 2019, both have 1) ✓ dropped. GE Bage 0-0 Monsoon (Série B 2022, both 1) ✓ dropped. Brasília x Taguatinga (Série A 2016, both 1) ✓ dropped. Bragantino 2017 Série B (1 match vs Tupi, Tupi has 2: the Bragantino match + Villa Nova match... wait Tupi 2017: matches = Bragantino 0-0 Tupi + Tupi's other? Earlier: Série B 2017 small: {'villa nova': 2, 'red bull bragantino-sp': 1, 'tupi-mg': 1}. Tupi has exactly 1 → Bragantino x Tupi: both teams have 1 match → dropped ✓. Villa Nova 2 matches: vs Brasil de Pelotas & CRB — both opponents have 38 → kept. Hmm, Villa Nova-MG (fake Vila Nova spelling) pollutes 2017 Série B standings slightly. Acceptable.\n\nWait, but what about the Chapecoense 2016 unscored canceled match? Chapecoense 2016 has 37 scored + 1 unscored. The unscored (vs Atlético-MG, Round 38) — after the plane crash it was canceled. It'll remain unscored ✓ correct. Atlético-MG 2016: 38 matches ✓. The unscored match doesn't affect standings (no score). But careful — my unscored-merge logic: BR-Football 2016 Série A — does it contain the Chapecoense x Atlético-MG match? If BR-Football has it WITH a score (wrong data — the match was never played; some datasets record 3-0 win or similar). If BR-Football has it scored, my merge would replace the unscored with a scored version — actually that might be \"correct\" per CBF decision? The CBF officially... the match was NOT played; CBF awarded... hmm, actually CBF declared Chapecoense champion of Copa do Brasil 2016; for Série A round 38, the match Atlético-MG x Chapecoense wasn't played. Let me check BR-Football for it later — if it merges, fine either way; the 2016 standings currently show Palmeiras 80 (real: 78!). Hmm wait — real 2016: Palmeiras 78 pts. We computed 80. That's because of the extra Brasília x Taguatinga match? No — that match involves neither Palmeiras nor its rivals... 381 matches with 380 + 1 fake. The fake doesn't change Palmeiras points. Palmeiras 80 vs real 78 — hmm, 2 extra points. Where from? Maybe novo vs Brasileirao dedup left a duplicate Palmeiras match, OR the source itself has an error, OR my memory of 78 is wrong. Let me verify: 2016 Palmeiras: W24 D8 L6? Hmm. Let me check real 2016: Palmeiras 78 pts (24W 6D 8L)? I genuinely don't remember exactly. Hmm — actually I recall 2016: Palmeiras champion, 78 points... Let me count from our data: matches where palmeiras played in 2016, count W/D/L.\n\nLet me do the fixes and then verify 2016/2022 carefully.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05bbd9ff8001uY2ETXqH0b3RG4","sessionID":"ses_fa45f1af7ffepwbxxISA0FiJ2d","messageID":"msg_05bbcba27001T8XGFaz6s3oCCp"}}
