{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788246862687,"sessionID":"ses_fa45f1af7ffepwbxxISA0FiJ2d","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_d9fed2d34e4d47eca69ebf91","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/stats.py","newString":"    return [\n        {\n            **r.to_dict(),\n            \"team\": team_display_name(r.team_key),\n            \"team_key\": r.team_key,\n        }\n        for r in records[:limit]\n    ]","oldString":"    return [\n        {\n            \"team\": team_display_name(r.team_key),\n            \"team_key\": r.team_key,\n            **r.to_dict(),\n        }\n        for r in records[:limit]\n    ]"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/stats.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/stats.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/stats.py\n@@ -223,11 +223,11 @@\n else:\n     records.sort(key=lambda r: (-r.points, -r.goal_difference))\n return [\n     {\n+        **r.to_dict(),\n         \"team\": team_display_name(r.team_key),\n         \"team_key\": r.team_key,\n-        **r.to_dict(),\n     }\n     for r in records[:limit]\n ]\n \n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/stats.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/stats.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/stats.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/stats.py\n@@ -223,11 +223,11 @@\n else:\n     records.sort(key=lambda r: (-r.points, -r.goal_difference))\n return [\n     {\n+        **r.to_dict(),\n         \"team\": team_display_name(r.team_key),\n         \"team_key\": r.team_key,\n-        **r.to_dict(),\n     }\n     for r in records[:limit]\n ]\n \n","additions":1,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"stats.py","time":{"start":1788246862682,"end":1788246862685}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Nearly all good. Issues to fix:\n\n1. **2013 Libertadores final \"unknown / drawn\"**: Olimpia 2-2 Atlético-MG aggregate — real winner: Atlético-MG on penalties. No penalties data. Acceptable to say drawn on aggregate — but let me improve the display to note \"decided on penalties (not in data)\". Actually the message \"unknown / drawn\" is fine but \"Flamengo None Athletico Paranaense\" for the NA row is ugly. Filter out editions with no season or no scores. Also 2013 shows first-leg aggregate team order — fine.\n\n2. **get_best_records summary shows team_key instead of display name**: \"gremio-rs - 63 goals\" — because best_records to_dict includes team_key and my summary uses row['team']... wait it prints row['team'] which should be display name. Looking at best_records: {\"team\": team_display_name(r.team_key), ...} — but output shows \"gremio-rs\"?! Oh wait — the summary line uses `row['team']`... The output shows 'gremio-rs'. team_display_name('gremio-rs') → 'Grêmio' via DISPLAY_NAMES. Hmm why raw key? OH — the dict has BOTH \"team\" and \"team_key\", and to_dict() from TeamRecord starts with \"team\": self.team_key! The **r.to_dict() spread AFTER \"team\" OVERWRITES the display name. Order in best_records: {\"team\": display, \"team_key\": key, **r.to_dict()} — to_dict has \"team\": self.team_key (the raw key) which overwrites. Fix: reorder the spread or rename TeamRecord.to_dict's field. I'll change best_records to put **r.to_dict() first then override team/team_key. Actually TeamRecord.to_dict returns \"team\": self.team_key — let me just fix in stats.best_records: build {\"team\": display, \"team_key\": key, **{k:v for k,v in r.to_dict().items() if k != 'team'}}. Simpler: {**r.to_dict(), \"team\": display, \"team_key\": key}.\n\n3. Gre-Nal 2019 ✓, Copa Libertadores finals ✓ (2013: penalties note). The \"None season\" edition — filter out matches without season in _finals_payload or skip legs without scores in summary detail. The NA final row (Flamengo-Athletico 2021): legs[0] with score None — detail \"Flamengo None Athletico Paranaense\". Filter: skip editions where no leg has a score. Also Libertadores 2021 final: the dataset has the final stage with 'NA' — the played final (Nov 2021, Flamengo won) — data has \"-\" goals. Just filter it out of finals listing (no result).\n\nHmm wait — actually let me check: Libertadores 2021 final — Flamengo x Athletico-PR. The file shows one row with NA. So 2021 final has no data. Filter no-score editions from _finals_payload.\n\n4. Also get_derby_matches season filter — works ✓.\n\nFix these two, then also check `get_competition_info` output and end-to-end stdio protocol test.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05bd1ab4b001NsdzORhuRKXzGf","sessionID":"ses_fa45f1af7ffepwbxxISA0FiJ2d","messageID":"msg_05bd12712001S0GHEiDI3CcJa8"}}
