e with smaller index. Since load order is brasileirao(1) → novo(2) → copa(3) → libert(4) → brfoot(5), earlier source = kept. Cup before BR-Football ✓. Within BR-Football, order = file row order.\n\nEdge: what if BOTH sides differ but each matches the other swapped (reversed fixture)? Skip — only one-side-differ pairs.\n\nLet me now also double check the earlier 'serra f c-es' vs 'serra' pair: bases \"serra f c\" vs \"serra\"; suffixes es vs None → one suffixless: core of \"serra f c\" minus legal {f? 'c'?} — \"f\" and \"c\" single letters... my LEGAL set has 'fc' but not 'f'/'c' separately. core = {serra, f, c} ⊆ {serra}? NO → fails → need static alias \"serra f c\" → (\"serra\",\"es\"). Hmm — or add single-letter legal tokens? Risky. Add manual statics for observed stragglers.\n\nPlan: implement learner, print learned aliases + residual unmatched fixture pairs, then add statics for stragglers.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05bd93b98001FqHgpA1IkyCXpv","sessionID":"ses_fa45f1af7ffepwbxxISA0FiJ2d","messageID":"msg_05bd69512001IGMi9Oc9Qlgztl"}}
