HER side is equal — both-sides-differ requires BOTH compatible ✓ strict. And pairs where one side is equal — same as existing buckets ✓ no new risk.\n\nOne more concern: the \"any\" bucket pair explosion — bucket size for (any, comp, season, date±1, score): typical weekend day, Série A, 6 matches, scores like 1-0 appearing 2-3 times → buckets of 2-4. Total pairs manageable ✓.\n\nBut WAIT — there's a subtle new false-merge risk in \"any\" buckets: two DIFFERENT matches, same comp/season/date/score, where home teams are compatible-but-different AND away teams compatible-but-different. E.g. \"atletico-mg 1-0 flamengo-rj\" and \"atletico-pr 1-0 flamengo\"? — compatible(atletico-mg, atletico-pr)? suffixes mg vs pr differ → reject ✓. \"gremio-rs 2-0 santos-sp\" and \"gremio 2-0 santos\"? — 'gremio' suffixless vs 'gremio-rs' compatible, 'santos' vs 'santos-sp' compatible → both-compatible → MERGE. Is that right? Same date ±1, same comp+season, same score, gremio-rs/gremio hosting, santos-sp/santos visiting — this IS the same match (both files recorded it) ✓ correct merge!\n\nOK — also the learning loop has a subtle issue: in \"any\" buckets, pairs where home equal & away differ → pairs=[(away...)]; where away equal & home differ → [(home...)]; where both differ → both. In any-buckets, unrelated matches with same home (impossible) — fine.\n\nNow also add the statics: afogados da ingazeira fc, esportivo bento goncalves, ceo varzeagrandense. And re-run.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05be0eacd0017TGD9c3f5AMunz","sessionID":"ses_fa45f1af7ffepwbxxISA0FiJ2d","messageID":"msg_05be06b85001LHriwIy1iCaFWs"}}
