o bernardo\", \"sp\"),\n \"sao jose rs\": (\"sao jose\", \"rs\"),\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/normalize.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/normalize.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/normalize.py\n@@ -204,8 +204,11 @@\n \"guarany de sobral\": (\"guarany\", \"ce\"),\n \"afogados da ingazeira fc\": (\"afogados\", \"pe\"),\n \"esportivo bento goncalves\": (\"esportivo\", \"rs\"),\n \"ceo varzeagrandense\": (\"operario\", \"mt\"),\n+\"peixe da amazonia\": (\"santos\", \"ap\"),\n+\"brasil de pelotas\": (\"brasil\", \"rs\"),\n+\"uniao\": (\"uniao de rondonopolis\", \"mt\"),\n \"inter de limeira\": (\"inter de limeira\", \"sp\"),\n \"sao bento\": (\"sao bento\", \"sp\"),\n \"sao bernardo\": (\"sao bernardo\", \"sp\"),\n \"sao jose rs\": (\"sao jose\", \"rs\"),\n","additions":3,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"normalize.py","time":{"start":1788247969416,"end":1788247969419}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Confirmed:\n1. \"Peixe da Amazonia - AP\" (cup, 2017) IS \"Santos AP\" (brfoot, same fixture vs Vasco 0-2 on 2017-02-09). So static: \"peixe da amazonia\" → (\"santos\",\"ap\") ✓. Both refer to the Macapá club Santos-AP. (Note line 658: \"Santos - AP\" vs \"Santos - SP\" — they even played each other in 2016! Great validation that 'santos-ap' must stay separate from 'santos-sp' ✓ my conflict rule handles.)\n\n2. 'uniao' learned as... \"uniao rondonopolis\" → ('uniao de rondonopolis','mt') ✓ — but the bad key in the 2020 fixture is 'uniao-mt' — base 'uniao' (WITH explicit uf mt, suffix stripped). Hmm: 'uniao-mt' comes from raw \"União - MT\"? wait no — the cup row shows 'uniao-mt vs atletico-go' source Brazilian_Cu — cup raw must be \"União - MT\" → base 'uniao' + uf mt. The brfoot row 'uniao de rondonopolis-mt' from \"Uniao Rondonopolis\". Learned alias: bad_base = 'uniao rondonopolis' → ('uniao de rondonopolis','mt')?? WAIT that's backwards from what I want! The learned entry maps \"uniao rondonopolis\" → (\"uniao de rondonopolis\",\"mt\") — but the CUP key is 'uniao-mt' (base 'uniao'). So the learner picked kept='uniao de rondonopolis-mt'?? That means the BRFOOT row loaded FIRST? No — cup is 3rd, brfoot 5th... UNLESS this fixture pair came from a different pair of matches! The learned alias 'uniao rondonopolis'→(...) must come from ANOTHER fixture where 'uniao rondonopolis' (brfoot, bad) paired with cup 'uniao de rondonopolis-mt'?? But cup raw for the club is \"União - MT\" hmm...\n\nLet me look: cup rows for União: \"União - MT\"? Hmm — actually earlier residual showed cup 'uniao de rondonopolis-mt' on 2020-02-07? No wait — the print above: '2020-02-06 uniao-mt vs atletico-go | Brazilian_Cu' and '2020-02-07 uniao de rondonopolis-mt vs atletico-go | BR-Football-'. So cup key = 'uniao-mt' (raw \"União - MT\"), brfoot key = 'uniao de rondonopolis-mt' (raw \"Uniao Rondonopolis\"). For the learner: kept = cup 'uniao-mt', bad = 'uniao de rondonopolis-mt' → learn bad_base 'uniao de rondonopolis' → ('uniao','mt') ✓ expected! But the learned shows 'uniao rondonopolis' → ('uniao de rondonopolis','mt') — INVERTED and different base! So there must be ANOTHER fixture pair that taught this: some cup row 'uniao de rondonopolis-mt' (cup raw \"União de Rondonópolis - MT\"?) vs brfoot 'uniao rondonopolis' (\"Uniao Rondonopolis\"?)... So the club appears in cup as BOTH \"União - MT\" AND \"União de Rondonópolis - MT\"?! And brfoot as both \"Uniao Rondonopolis\" and ...? Messy source. The learned chain: 'uniao rondonopolis' → 'uniao de rondonopolis-mt' ✓ good. But cup's 'uniao-mt' still separate.\n\nFix: static \"uniao\" → (\"uniao de rondonopolis\",\"mt\")? Hmm — \"uniao\" could be other Uniões (União-SC? Novo Hamburgo?). In this dataset, base 'uniao' appears only as União-MT (cup) — hmm, brfoot \"Uniao Rondonopolis\" has base 'uniao rondonopolis' (not bare 'uniao'). Wait, does brfoot have bare \"Uniao\"? From the nosuffix list earlier: 'Uniao Rondonopolis' only. And cup \"União - MT\" → bare 'uniao'. So static \"uniao\" → (\"uniao de rondonopolis\",\"mt\") is safe for this dataset ✓.\n\n3. 'brasil de pelotas' — re-add static → (\"brasil\",\"rs\").\n\nLet me add these three statics and rerun. Then finalize: the remaining residuals are all genuine source errors/different clubs — acceptable (15 pairs out of 16.7k matches = 0.09% noise).","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05be28e7b001cq9BpJocYytIE3","sessionID":"ses_fa45f1af7ffepwbxxISA0FiJ2d","messageID":"msg_05be200fa001wgYrp03ttpekcT"}}
