{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788248018128,"sessionID":"ses_fa45f1af7ffepwbxxISA0FiJ2d","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_e8ed918ce2564abbbb5c254e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"\"\"\"Shared pytest fixtures for the Brazilian Soccer MCP test suite.\n\nBDD GWT background: the match and player data is loaded once per test\nsession (loading takes ~2 seconds because of the two-phase alias-learning\nload), so every scenario reuses the same :class:`~data_loader.SoccerData`\ninstance via the ``data`` fixture.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom data_loader import SoccerData, get_data\n\n\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"session\")\ndef data() -> SoccerData:\n    \"\"\"Given: the full dataset is loaded and deduplicated.\"\"\"\n    return get_data()\n","filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/conftest.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/conftest.py","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"conftest.py","time":{"start":1788248018122,"end":1788248018126}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Data pipeline finalized:\n- 16,745 deduped matches (from ~24k raw rows across 5 files)\n- All verifiable standings match real history\n- Load: 1.8s (two-phase), lookups instant\n\nNow write the BDD GWT pytest tests. TASK.md specifies BDD GWT structure. I'll write test files:\n\n1. `test_normalization.py` — team name variations, dates, competition aliases\n2. `test_match_queries.py` — match search scenarios\n3. `test_team_queries.py` — team stats, h2h, best records\n4. `test_player_queries.py` — player search scenarios\n5. `test_competition_queries.py` — standings, finals, info\n6. `test_statistics.py` — aggregates, biggest wins, derbies\n7. `test_mcp_server.py` — MCP protocol-level tests (list tools, call tools async)\n\nBDD GWT structure: organize with Gherkin-style docstrings and Given/When/Then comments in each test. Use a session-scoped fixture for the loaded data.\n\nLet me write conftest.py with the shared fixture, then the test files. Also pyproject.toml for pytest config.\n\nKey scenarios to cover (≥20 sample questions from the spec):\n1. \"Show me all Flamengo vs Fluminense matches\" ✓\n2. \"What matches did Palmeiras play in 2023?\" ✓\n3. \"Find all Copa do Brasil finals\" ✓\n4. \"What is Corinthians' home record in 2022?\" ✓\n5. \"Which team scored the most goals in Serie A 2023?\" ✓\n6. \"Compare Palmeiras and Santos head-to-head\" ✓\n7. \"Find all Brazilian players\" (top-rated) ✓\n8. \"Who are the highest-rated players at Santos?\" ✓\n9. \"Show me all forwards from São Paulo FC\"? — São Paulo not in FIFA! Use \"Grêmio forwards\" or similar; test that São Paulo returns graceful empty. \n10. \"Who won the 2019 Brasileirão?\" ✓\n11. \"Which teams were relegated in 2020?\" ✓\n12. \"What's the average goals per match in the Brasileirão?\" ✓\n13. \"Which team has the best away record?\" ✓\n14. \"Show me the biggest wins in the dataset\" ✓\n15. \"When did Flamengo last play Corinthians?\" ✓ (most recent)\n16. \"What was the score?\" (of that match) ✓\n17. \"Who is Gabriel Jesus?\" (player by name — Gabriel Barbosa absent from FIFA, Gabriel Jesus present) ✓\n18. \"Which players play for Grêmio?\" ✓\n19. \"Show me all derbies in 2023\" ✓ (derby matches)\n20. \"What competitions has Palmeiras played in?\" ✓\n21. Cross-file: club squad + match record ✓\n22. \"Show the 2018 Copa Libertadores final\" ✓\n23. Team name normalization variants ✓\n24. Ambiguity handling \"Atletico\" ✓\n25. Date range queries ✓\n26. Stage queries (\"final\") ✓\n\nMCP protocol tests: list_tools contains 16 tools; call_tool returns content; call search_matches + get_standings via async.\n\nAlso performance tests: simple lookup < 2s, aggregate < 5s (measure with data already loaded — the load is one-time; per spec \"simple lookups respond in < 2 seconds\" — including first-call load? 1.8s load + query < 2s total. I'll assert query times with warm data, plus assert total cold load < 5s maybe. Keep performance test light: warm query < 2s, aggregate < 5s.)\n\nLet me write conftest.py first.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05be34cc4001zBiwA3n0YHlsGb","sessionID":"ses_fa45f1af7ffepwbxxISA0FiJ2d","messageID":"msg_05be2c088001fv29eNeJpEdFFr"}}
