s(matches)\n highlights = champion_and_relegated(table)\n scored = [m for m in matches if m.score is not None]\n expected = LEAGUE_FULL_SEASON.get(comp)\n-partial = expected is not None and len(scored) < expected * 0.98\n+partial = expected is not None and len(scored) < expected\n lines = [f\"{comp} {season_val} standings (calculated from {len(scored)} matches):\"]\n for row in table:\n     marker = \"\"\n     if row[\"position\"] == 1:\n","additions":1,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"server.py","time":{"start":1788248364595,"end":1788248364598}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The 2023 season has 377 matches; my threshold is `len(scored) < expected * 0.98` → 377 < 380*0.98 = 372.4? No — 377 > 372.4 → not flagged. The 2023 data is genuinely missing only 3 matches, but those 3 flipped the championship (Grêmio shown above Palmeiras though real champion was Palmeiras). Hmm — should I lower the threshold to catch this? A full season is 380; missing 3 (0.8%) flipped the title. Lowering to 0.99 (375.2) would flag 2023 (377 < 375.2? NO — 377 > 375.2). 380*0.99=376.2; 377 > 376.2 → still not flagged. Need < 380 i.e. exact: flag when scored < expected. But then a single missing match (data error) would flag \"partial\" — that's honest actually! If the dataset doesn't have the full 380, say so. But is \"partial\" the right word when 377/380? \"complete_data\": scored == expected. Let me flag partial when scored < expected (strict). For Série A seasons with the 2009 double-recording (381 raw but unique 380) — scored count is what matters ✓.\n\nAlso check: 2016 was 380 ✓; some earlier seasons (2003: 552 = complete for 24 teams ✓ expected is 380 for Série A... WAIT — 2003 had 24 teams → 552 matches! My LEAGUE_FULL_SEASON uses fixed 380 for Série A — WRONG for 2003-2005 (22-24 teams!). 2003: 552, 2004: 552? (24 teams), 2005: 462 (22 teams). So a fixed 380 expectation would wrongly flag 2003-2005 as \"partial\" (552 > 380 → not partial ✓ since 552 > 380... only LESS flags). But 2003 has MORE than 380 — not flagged ✓ OK directionally. But the real completeness rule for Série A 2006+ is 380. 2003-2005 have more matches — fine, never flagged.\n\nSérie B: expected 380 ✓ (20 teams since 2006; 2014+ all 20 teams ✓). Série C: format varied (I guessed 190). 2014 partial (81), 2015 (157), 2016 (181)... those would flag as partial ✓ correct (they ARE partial). But some Série C seasons might have a different full format (e.g. 2019 Série C: 20 teams → 160? hmm, actually Série C 2019 format: 20 teams, single round-robin = 190 matches then playoffs. BR-Football's Série C data is partial regardless. Fine — flagging partial is honest.\n\nChange rule: `partial = expected is not None and len(scored) < expected`. 2023: 377 < 380 → partial ✓. 2019: 380 → complete ✓.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05be89626001RcNItrBlKOcwqY","sessionID":"ses_fa45f1af7ffepwbxxISA0FiJ2d","messageID":"msg_05be80997001SL4oojbRBzgVHi"}}
