{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788248397825,"sessionID":"ses_fa45f1af7ffepwbxxISA0FiJ2d","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call_7252906066a142928e053113","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/server.py","newString":"def _resolve_team_arg(\n    query: Optional[str], data: SoccerData\n) -> tuple[Optional[str], Optional[dict]]:\n    if not query:\n        return None, None\n    exact_key = canonical_team_key(query)\n    if exact_key and exact_key in data.teams:\n        return exact_key, None\n    candidates = data.find_team(query)\n    if not candidates:\n        return None, {\n            \"error\": f\"No team matching '{query}' was found in the dataset.\",\n        }","oldString":"def _resolve_team_arg(\n    query: Optional[str], data: SoccerData\n) -> tuple[Optional[str], Optional[dict]]:\n    if not query:\n        return None, None\n    candidates = data.find_team(query)\n    if not candidates:\n        return None, {\n            \"error\": f\"No team matching '{query}' was found in the dataset.\",\n        }"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/server.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/server.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/server.py\n@@ -93,8 +93,11 @@\n     query: Optional[str], data: SoccerData\n ) -> tuple[Optional[str], Optional[dict]]:\n     if not query:\n         return None, None\n+    exact_key = canonical_team_key(query)\n+    if exact_key and exact_key in data.teams:\n+        return exact_key, None\n     candidates = data.find_team(query)\n     if not candidates:\n         return None, {\n             \"error\": f\"No team matching '{query}' was found in the dataset.\",\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/server.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/server.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/server.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/server.py\n@@ -93,8 +93,11 @@\n     query: Optional[str], data: SoccerData\n ) -> tuple[Optional[str], Optional[dict]]:\n     if not query:\n         return None, None\n+    exact_key = canonical_team_key(query)\n+    if exact_key and exact_key in data.teams:\n+        return exact_key, None\n     candidates = data.find_team(query)\n     if not candidates:\n         return None, {\n             \"error\": f\"No team matching '{query}' was found in the dataset.\",\n","additions":3,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"server.py","time":{"start":1788248397822,"end":1788248397824}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Three failures:\n\n1. `test_dotted_abbreviations_collapse` — \"A.s.a. - RN\" should equal \"Asa - AL\"?? Wait, my test is wrong: Asa-AL is the Alagoas club; A.s.a.-RN is... hmm, actually \"A.s.a. - RN\" — ASA is the ALAGOAS club (Arapiraca)! The Copa file has \"A.s.a. - RN\"?? That looks like a data error in the Copa file (should be -AL). Hmm wait, earlier data exploration showed: 'A.b.c. - RN', 'A.s.a. - AL', 'ABC - RN', 'Abc - RN', 'Asa - AL'. So \"A.s.a. - AL\" exists (correct), and my test asserted 'A.s.a. - RN' == 'Asa - AL' — wrong test premise. There's no 'A.s.a. - RN'. Fix the test: assert canonical_team_key(\"A.s.a. - AL\") == canonical_team_key(\"Asa - AL\") == \"asa-al\". And the ABC part is fine.\n\n2. `test_derbies_in_2023` — \"too many values to unpack (expected 3)\" at test_statistics.py:141: `{name for _, _, name in result[\"data\"][\"derbies_known\"]}` — derbies_known is `[name for _, _, name in DERBY_PAIRS]` — a list of NAMES (strings), not tuples. Iterating a string with `_, _, name` unpacks chars. Fix test: `set(result[\"data\"][\"derbies_known\"])`.\n\n3. `test_head_to_head_between_teams_that_never_met` — \"Nacional (URU)\" query → find_team resolves... hmm, the resolve failed → returned error dict (no 'data'). Why? find_team(\"Nacional (URU)\") → canonical → \"nacional-uru\" ✓ should be in teams (Libertadores). But the AMBIGUITY check: candidates: exact \"nacional-uru\" + substring matches \"nacional-par\", \"nacional-am\"... top.match_count vs second.match_count: nacional-uru has maybe 12 matches; nacional-par has 10 → ratio < 5 → AMBIGUOUS → error. Hmm! That's the ambiguity path kicking in for legit distinct-but-similar names. For \"Nacional (URU)\" the user explicitly disambiguated with the country code! The canonical key is EXACT \"nacional-uru\" — when the query resolves to an EXACT known key, we should use it without ambiguity check. Fix `_resolve_team_arg`: first check `data.teams.get(canonical_team_key(query))` — if the exact key exists, return it immediately (no ambiguity). The substring-candidate logic only applies when there's no exact hit. That's better UX overall: \"Nacional (URU)\" → exact; \"Nacional\" → ambiguous candidates.\n\nLet me fix all three.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05be917f800194zCvd2F2gs4Zw","sessionID":"ses_fa45f1af7ffepwbxxISA0FiJ2d","messageID":"msg_05be8b55f0012ivR6NDN2wllXs"}}
