{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788248481906,"sessionID":"ses_fa45f1af7ffepwbxxISA0FiJ2d","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_d43d340baa5541a9bc0de6be","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"\"\"\"Manual end-to-end check: drive the MCP server over stdio JSON-RPC.\n\nNot part of the pytest suite (keeps the suite fast); run with::\n\n    python e2e_stdio_check.py\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\n\n\ndef main() -> int:\n    proc = subprocess.Popen(\n        [sys.executable, \"server.py\"],\n        stdin=subprocess.PIPE,\n        stdout=subprocess.PIPE,\n        stderr=subprocess.PIPE,\n        text=True,\n        bufsize=1,\n    )\n\n    def send(payload: dict) -> None:\n        proc.stdin.write(json.dumps(payload) + \"\\n\")\n        proc.stdin.flush()\n\n    def recv() -> dict:\n        line = proc.stdout.readline()\n        if not line:\n            raise RuntimeError(\"server closed stdout: \" + proc.stderr.read())\n        return json.loads(line)\n\n    send({\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"id\": 1, \"method\": \"initialize\", \"params\": {\n        \"protocolVersion\": \"2025-06-18\",\n        \"capabilities\": {},\n        \"clientInfo\": {\"name\": \"e2e-check\", \"version\": \"1.0\"},\n    }})\n    init = recv()\n    assert \"serverInfo\" in init[\"result\"], init\n    print(\"initialize ->\", init[\"result\"][\"serverInfo\"][\"name\"])\n\n    send({\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"method\": \"notifications/initialized\"})\n    send({\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"id\": 2, \"method\": \"tools/list\"})\n    tools = recv()\n    names = [t[\"name\"] for t in tools[\"result\"][\"tools\"]]\n    print(f\"tools/list -> {len(names)} tools\")\n    assert \"search_matches\" in names and \"get_standings\" in names\n\n    send({\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"id\": 3, \"method\": \"tools/call\", \"params\": {\n        \"name\": \"get_standings\",\n        \"arguments\": {\"competition\": \"brasileirao\", \"season\": 2019},\n    }})\n    result = recv()\n    text = result[\"result\"][\"content\"][0][\"text\"]\n    payload = json.loads(text)\n    champion = payload[\"data\"][\"champion\"]\n    print(\"get_standings 2019 -> champion:\", champion)\n    assert champion == \"Flamengo\", payload\n\n    send({\"jsonrpc\": \"2.0\", \"id\": 4, \"method\": \"tools/call\", \"params\": {\n        \"name\": \"get_head_to_head\",\n        \"arguments\": {\"team_a\": \"Flamengo\", \"team_b\": \"Fluminense\"},\n    }})\n    result = recv()\n    payload = json.loads(result[\"result\"][\"content\"][0][\"text\"])\n    print(\"head_to_head Fla-Flu ->\", payload[\"data\"][\"total_meetings\"], \"meetings\")\n    assert payload[\"data\"][\"total_meetings\"] > 30\n\n    proc.stdin.close()\n    proc.wait(timeout=10)\n    print(\"E2E OK\")\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    raise SystemExit(main())\n","filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/e2e_stdio_check.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-7ooj92cj/retort-80ffd0e4ce9f/e2e_stdio_check.py","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"e2e_stdio_check.py","time":{"start":1788248481896,"end":1788248481904}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"**95 tests passed in 2.25s.** \n\nHmm wait, 2.25s total? The data load takes ~1.8s once per session... and all 95 tests in 2.25s — the session fixture loads once (1.8s) + tests run fast. \n\nHmm — but wait, the collect-only grep -c \"::\" gave 0 because `-q` collect output format differs. Whatever — 95 passed.\n\nNow the remaining work:\n1. End-to-end stdio server verification (spawn `python server.py` and speak MCP over stdio — or at least verify it starts and responds to initialize).\n2. requirements.txt.\n3. README.md update.\n4. Final cleanup review of the code (check for leftover issues, e.g. `get_derby_matches` team filter uses `next(k for k, v in known.items() if v == d[\"derby\"])` — that's O(n) per match and could StopIteration if derby name not in known... it is. OK but fragile. Let me review server.py once more).\n5. Check flake8-level cleanliness (no unused imports). Let me run a quick lint check with python -m pyflakes if available, or compileall.\n\nLet me check server.py for unused imports: I imported `parse_date`, `canonical_team_key`, `team_display_name`, `DERBY_PAIRS`, `resolve_competition` — all used. `date` used in sort lambdas. `SoccerData` used in type hints. `SERIE_B/SERIE_C` used in LEAGUE_FULL_SEASON. `team_record` used in get_club_players. `finals` used. `champion_and_relegated` used. `best_records, biggest_wins, competition_aggregates, derby_matches, head_to_head, standings` used. OK.\n\nIn data_loader: imports — `date` used in sort key (`m.date or date.min`) ✓; `replace` ✓; `team_display_name` — hmm, is it used in data_loader? TeamEntry.display uses team_display_name ✓. `strip_accents` used in _norm_text ✓. `normalize_round` ✓.\n\nIn `_load_libertadores`: `season = parse_int(row[\"season\"])` then `season=season` — fine. There's an unused variable? `season` used ✓.\n\ntest_mcp_server.py imports `get_team_stats` — used in composite perf test ✓. `json` ✓. `asyncio` ✓.\n\nNow let me do the stdio end-to-end test: run `python server.py` as subprocess, send initialize + tools/list + tools/call JSON-RPC messages over stdin, read stdout. The MCP stdio protocol uses newline-delimited JSON (mcp 2.x — let me verify: the stdio transport in MCP Python SDK uses newline-delimited JSON messages (one JSON per line).","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05bea605e001q1P7zEhGx7tcF6","sessionID":"ses_fa45f1af7ffepwbxxISA0FiJ2d","messageID":"msg_05be9d33a00195FM660c8Y2HXJ"}}
